{"parentUuid":"cd126745-7896-4680-928f-508b85d67c6a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"355cfc4f-9d72-4bb3-8805-f2dd57c05477","agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TvqvCYvyjCYP9LBGuyaoVH","type":"tool_result","content":"The docs describe the List models response object at the top level as containing only two fields: `data` (an array) and `object`, where object has \"Allowed values: `list`\".\n\nThe per-model field names aren't itemized in the List models schema section, but the example response for that endpoint shows each entry with:\n\n- `id`\n- `object`\n- `created`\n- `owned_by`\n- `active`\n- `context_window`\n- `public_apps`\n\nThe Retrieve model endpoint documents a smaller set explicitly: `created`, `id`, `object` (described as \"The object type, which is always \"model\"\"), and `owned_by` (\"The organization that owns the model.\"). Its example response, however, adds `active`, `context_window`, `public_apps`, and `max_completion_tokens` — so `max_completion_tokens` appears in the retrieve example but not in the list example shown.\n\nOn pricing/free-tier: no. Nothing in the models endpoints returns cost, rate-limit tier, or free-tier data. The only tier-related concept mentioned anywhere on this page is `service_tier` in chat/responses requests, with values such as \"auto, on_demand, flex, performance, null\" — that's a request-time latency/priority setting, not model pricing metadata."}]},"uuid":"3d1b2dec-187d-4620-9d51-3e6af95f8faa","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:44:46.608Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":1526736,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The docs describe the List models response object at the top level as containing only two fields: `data` (an array) and `object`, where object has \"Allowed values: `list`\".\n\nThe per-model field names aren't itemized in the List models schema section, but the example response for that endpoint shows each entry with:\n\n- `id`\n- `object`\n- `created`\n- `owned_by`\n- `active`\n- `context_window`\n- `public_apps`\n\nThe Retrieve model endpoint documents a smaller set explicitly: `created`, `id`, `object` (described as \"The object type, which is always \"model\"\"), and `owned_by` (\"The organization that owns the model.\"). Its example response, however, adds `active`, `context_window`, `public_apps`, and `max_completion_tokens` — so `max_completion_tokens` appears in the retrieve example but not in the list example shown.\n\nOn pricing/free-tier: no. Nothing in the models endpoints returns cost, rate-limit tier, or free-tier data. The only tier-related concept mentioned anywhere on this page is `service_tier` in chat/responses requests, with values such as \"auto, on_demand, flex, performance, null\" — that's a request-time latency/priority setting, not model pricing metadata.","durationMs":9084,"url":"https://console.groq.com/docs/api-reference"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cd126745-7896-4680-928f-508b85d67c6a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
