{"parentUuid":"52b6d515-19bf-4194-a66d-d49c3b1af26c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","message":{"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeeEsJcMbPsthfRfGZkq2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012poJzcvKzX7M2ewZPPmwSG","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.together.ai/reference/models-1","prompt":"What exact fields does Together AI's GET /v1/models return per model? Does the response include a pricing object (e.g. pricing.input, pricing.output, pricing.hourly, pricing.base), context_length, type, and organization? Quote exact field names."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6861,"cache_read_input_tokens":167346,"output_tokens":596,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":305},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6861},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":596,"cache_read_input_tokens":167346,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6861,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6861,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CeeEsGyt1fswLUYUru8ee","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d83b04b6-53c0-461b-b46d-b6334c7bcec9","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:44:55.526Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"d83b04b6-53c0-461b-b46d-b6334c7bcec9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"355cfc4f-9d72-4bb3-8805-f2dd57c05477","agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012poJzcvKzX7M2ewZPPmwSG","type":"tool_result","content":"Yes — the OpenAPI spec confirms all of those. `GET /models` returns an array (`ModelInfoList`) of `ModelInfo` objects.\n\n**Required fields:** `id`, `object`, `created`, `type`\n\n**Optional fields:** `display_name`, `organization`, `link`, `license`, `context_length`, `pricing`\n\nField details:\n- `object` — \"The object type, which is always `model`.\"\n- `created` — integer timestamp (example: `1692896905`)\n- `type` — an enum of `chat`, `language`, `code`, `image`, `embedding`, `moderation`, `rerank`\n- `context_length` — integer (example: `2048`)\n- `organization` — string (example: `Austism`)\n- `id` — string (example: `Austism/chronos-hermes-13b`)\n\n**Pricing object** — yes, it's present and references a `Pricing` schema whose required fields are `hourly`, `input`, `output`, `base`, `finetune`. There is also an optional `cached_input` field. Example values in the spec: `input` and `output` at `0.3`, `cached_input` at `0.2`, and `base`, `finetune`, `hourly` at `0`.\n\nOne caveat worth noting: the query parameter `dedicated` is described as a filter \"to only return dedicated models,\" so results vary depending on whether you pass it."}]},"uuid":"68d25fee-66fb-4ef5-bba6-517ef1a02aae","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:45:06.990Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":6219,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"Yes — the OpenAPI spec confirms all of those. `GET /models` returns an array (`ModelInfoList`) of `ModelInfo` objects.\n\n**Required fields:** `id`, `object`, `created`, `type`\n\n**Optional fields:** `display_name`, `organization`, `link`, `license`, `context_length`, `pricing`\n\nField details:\n- `object` — \"The object type, which is always `model`.\"\n- `created` — integer timestamp (example: `1692896905`)\n- `type` — an enum of `chat`, `language`, `code`, `image`, `embedding`, `moderation`, `rerank`\n- `context_length` — integer (example: `2048`)\n- `organization` — string (example: `Austism`)\n- `id` — string (example: `Austism/chronos-hermes-13b`)\n\n**Pricing object** — yes, it's present and references a `Pricing` schema whose required fields are `hourly`, `input`, `output`, `base`, `finetune`. There is also an optional `cached_input` field. Example values in the spec: `input` and `output` at `0.3`, `cached_input` at `0.2`, and `base`, `finetune`, `hourly` at `0`.\n\nOne caveat worth noting: the query parameter `dedicated` is described as a filter \"to only return dedicated models,\" so results vary depending on whether you pass it.","durationMs":8141,"url":"https://docs.together.ai/reference/models-1"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d83b04b6-53c0-461b-b46d-b6334c7bcec9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"52b6d515-19bf-4194-a66d-d49c3b1af26c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"355cfc4f-9d72-4bb3-8805-f2dd57c05477","agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nouo44VMUtpLk5Tg6XCZ6y","type":"tool_result","content":"Each model object in the `GET /models` response has exactly three required fields:\n\n- **`id`** (string) — \"The model identifier, which can be referenced in the API endpoints.\"\n- **`object`** (string) — always the literal value `model`; described as \"The object type, which is always \"model\".\"\n- **`owned_by`** (string) — \"The organization that owns the model.\"\n\nThese sit inside a top-level wrapper with `object` set to `list` and a `data` array of model entries. The sample response shows entries like `deepseek-v4-flash` and `deepseek-v4-pro`, both owned by `deepseek`.\n\n**No pricing or free tier data is returned.** The endpoint only \"provides basic information about each one such as the owner and availability.\" For cost details, the docs point you elsewhere — they direct readers to \"Check Models & Pricing for our currently supported models,\" which links to a separate `/quick_start/pricing` page."}]},"uuid":"189cb800-46bd-4897-928a-6c0df25d4f42","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:45:08.493Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":29721,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"Each model object in the `GET /models` response has exactly three required fields:\n\n- **`id`** (string) — \"The model identifier, which can be referenced in the API endpoints.\"\n- **`object`** (string) — always the literal value `model`; described as \"The object type, which is always \"model\".\"\n- **`owned_by`** (string) — \"The organization that owns the model.\"\n\nThese sit inside a top-level wrapper with `object` set to `list` and a `data` array of model entries. The sample response shows entries like `deepseek-v4-flash` and `deepseek-v4-pro`, both owned by `deepseek`.\n\n**No pricing or free tier data is returned.** The endpoint only \"provides basic information about each one such as the owner and availability.\" For cost details, the docs point you elsewhere — they direct readers to \"Check Models & Pricing for our currently supported models,\" which links to a separate `/quick_start/pricing` page.","durationMs":11150,"url":"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/api/list-models"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"52b6d515-19bf-4194-a66d-d49c3b1af26c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
