{"parentUuid":"d5dbf751-e7ce-45a1-bd0f-b39790c48738","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","message":{"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeeEtvA3oNXkRM5zMDU6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012TEP1eibr95NpzFUixrLCL","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/api/","prompt":"What fields does Mistral's GET /v1/models return per model? Look for: id, object, created, owned_by, capabilities (completion_chat, function_calling, vision), name, description, max_context_length, aliases, deprecation, deprecation_replacement_model, default_model_temperature, type. Does it include pricing or free tier info?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1430,"cache_read_input_tokens":174207,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1430,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CeeEttgFHpcAqK2PZyVxy","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1e9875b0-2971-4e60-b88a-3f2e1ce7f7d3","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:45:15.391Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"1e9875b0-2971-4e60-b88a-3f2e1ce7f7d3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"355cfc4f-9d72-4bb3-8805-f2dd57c05477","agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012TEP1eibr95NpzFUixrLCL","type":"tool_result","content":"The page content provided doesn't answer your question. It documents only the **Chat Completions** endpoint (`POST /v1/chat/completions`) — its request body fields (`messages`, `model`, `temperature`, `tools`, `stream`, etc.) and its 200 response shape (`choices`, `created`, `id`, `model`, `object`, `usage`).\n\nThe Models endpoint appears only as navigation links and a cross-reference. The chat docs mention you can use the \"[List Available Models](/api#tag/models/operation/list_models_v1_models_get) API to see all of your available models,\" and separately link to a \"Model overview\" page — but no schema for the models response is shown here.\n\nSo I can't confirm any of the fields you listed (id, object, created, owned_by, capabilities, aliases, deprecation, default_model_temperature, type, etc.), nor whether pricing or free-tier data is returned. The only pricing-adjacent detail on this page is under `prompt_cache_key`, which notes that \"Cached tokens are billed at 10% of the standard input token price\" — that's about chat billing, not the models listing.\n\nTo get the actual field list, you'd need the `/api/endpoint/models` reference page or the OpenAPI spec linked as \"Download OpenAPI Spec\" (`/openapi.yaml`), where the `list_models_v1_models_get` operation schema would be defined."}]},"uuid":"132dbce1-a204-4672-86a4-82a2a8074130","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:45:27.320Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":2161186,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The page content provided doesn't answer your question. It documents only the **Chat Completions** endpoint (`POST /v1/chat/completions`) — its request body fields (`messages`, `model`, `temperature`, `tools`, `stream`, etc.) and its 200 response shape (`choices`, `created`, `id`, `model`, `object`, `usage`).\n\nThe Models endpoint appears only as navigation links and a cross-reference. The chat docs mention you can use the \"[List Available Models](/api#tag/models/operation/list_models_v1_models_get) API to see all of your available models,\" and separately link to a \"Model overview\" page — but no schema for the models response is shown here.\n\nSo I can't confirm any of the fields you listed (id, object, created, owned_by, capabilities, aliases, deprecation, default_model_temperature, type, etc.), nor whether pricing or free-tier data is returned. The only pricing-adjacent detail on this page is under `prompt_cache_key`, which notes that \"Cached tokens are billed at 10% of the standard input token price\" — that's about chat billing, not the models listing.\n\nTo get the actual field list, you'd need the `/api/endpoint/models` reference page or the OpenAPI spec linked as \"Download OpenAPI Spec\" (`/openapi.yaml`), where the `list_models_v1_models_get` operation schema would be defined.","durationMs":8217,"url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/api/"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1e9875b0-2971-4e60-b88a-3f2e1ce7f7d3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"d5dbf751-e7ce-45a1-bd0f-b39790c48738","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"355cfc4f-9d72-4bb3-8805-f2dd57c05477","agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Tcfrw6ERVZkMhGNeuvRRm","type":"tool_result","content":"The page documents the control-plane endpoint, not the OpenAI-compatible one. The path is `get /v1/accounts/{account_id}/models`, operation ID `Gateway_ListModels`, served from `https://api.fireworks.ai` with bearer auth.\n\n**Response envelope** (`gatewayListModelsResponse`): `models`, `nextPageToken`, and `totalSize`.\n\n**Query parameters:** `pageSize` (docs note \"The maximum page_size is 200\"), `pageToken`, `filter`, `orderBy`, and `readMask`.\n\n**Per-model fields** (`gatewayModel`) relevant to your question:\n\n- **State** — yes: `state`, typed as `gatewayModelState` with enum values `STATE_UNSPECIFIED`, `UPLOADING`, `READY`. There's also `status` for error detail.\n- **Context length** — yes, but camelCase: `contextLength` and `trainingContextLength`, both described as \"The maximum context length supported by the model.\"\n- **Image input** — yes: `supportsImageInput`, plus `supportsTools`.\n- **Deprecation date** — yes: `deprecationDate`, a `typeDate` (year/month/day), described as the date \"when the serverless deployment of the model will be taken down.\"\n- **Pricing** — not directly on the model object here. Pricing appears nested under `serverlessModes[].skuInfos`, using `gatewaySKUInfo` (`sku`, `amount` as `typeMoney`, `unit` e.g. \"1M tokens\"). Notably these are \"sourced live from Orb on the read path\" and marked read-only; the schema comment says they're \"never persisted\" and \"only computed live at read time,\" populated by ListServerlessModels.\n\n**Other notable fields:** `name`, `displayName`, `description`, `createTime`, `updateTime`, `kind`, `githubUrl`, `huggingFaceUrl`, `baseModelDetails`, `peftDetails`, `public`, `conversationConfig`, `supportsServerless`, `supportsLora`, `defaultDraftModel`, `deployedModelRefs`, `cluster`, `calibrated`, `encryptionState`, and tuning flags like `supervisedLoraTunable` and `rlFullParameterTunable` (the older `tunable` and `rlTunable` are marked deprecated for V1 only).\n\nField naming is camelCase throughout — this is a resource-management API returning `name` values like `accounts/my-account/models/my-model`, distinct from an OpenAI-style `/inference/v1/models` listing, which isn't covered on this page."}]},"uuid":"ecc2920f-57c7-48bd-b740-4c7b5befce1b","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:45:31.176Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":33920,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The page documents the control-plane endpoint, not the OpenAI-compatible one. The path is `get /v1/accounts/{account_id}/models`, operation ID `Gateway_ListModels`, served from `https://api.fireworks.ai` with bearer auth.\n\n**Response envelope** (`gatewayListModelsResponse`): `models`, `nextPageToken`, and `totalSize`.\n\n**Query parameters:** `pageSize` (docs note \"The maximum page_size is 200\"), `pageToken`, `filter`, `orderBy`, and `readMask`.\n\n**Per-model fields** (`gatewayModel`) relevant to your question:\n\n- **State** — yes: `state`, typed as `gatewayModelState` with enum values `STATE_UNSPECIFIED`, `UPLOADING`, `READY`. There's also `status` for error detail.\n- **Context length** — yes, but camelCase: `contextLength` and `trainingContextLength`, both described as \"The maximum context length supported by the model.\"\n- **Image input** — yes: `supportsImageInput`, plus `supportsTools`.\n- **Deprecation date** — yes: `deprecationDate`, a `typeDate` (year/month/day), described as the date \"when the serverless deployment of the model will be taken down.\"\n- **Pricing** — not directly on the model object here. Pricing appears nested under `serverlessModes[].skuInfos`, using `gatewaySKUInfo` (`sku`, `amount` as `typeMoney`, `unit` e.g. \"1M tokens\"). Notably these are \"sourced live from Orb on the read path\" and marked read-only; the schema comment says they're \"never persisted\" and \"only computed live at read time,\" populated by ListServerlessModels.\n\n**Other notable fields:** `name`, `displayName`, `description`, `createTime`, `updateTime`, `kind`, `githubUrl`, `huggingFaceUrl`, `baseModelDetails`, `peftDetails`, `public`, `conversationConfig`, `supportsServerless`, `supportsLora`, `defaultDraftModel`, `deployedModelRefs`, `cluster`, `calibrated`, `encryptionState`, and tuning flags like `supervisedLoraTunable` and `rlFullParameterTunable` (the older `tunable` and `rlTunable` are marked deprecated for V1 only).\n\nField naming is camelCase throughout — this is a resource-management API returning `name` values like `accounts/my-account/models/my-model`, distinct from an OpenAI-style `/inference/v1/models` listing, which isn't covered on this page.","durationMs":14115,"url":"https://docs.fireworks.ai/api-reference/list-models"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d5dbf751-e7ce-45a1-bd0f-b39790c48738","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
