{"parentUuid":"2671113e-e223-4397-89cc-a87be7247b86","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","message":{"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeeF1KvTTvyw5uLJJawRM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E1hjbKpVo9J6SRboWhCAMN","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api-reference/limits","prompt":"What are the rate limits for :free models on OpenRouter? Describe free model rate limits (requests per minute, per day), the credit-balance thresholds, and what the /api/v1/key or /api/v1/credits endpoint returns. Also describe model variant suffixes like :free, :nitro, :floor, :online, :extended, :thinking."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1830,"cache_read_input_tokens":184643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1830,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CeeF1JY7g2owNexGzmRDN","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"5fbe22a3-d28e-4629-84fd-0979895a45be","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:46:43.975Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"5fbe22a3-d28e-4629-84fd-0979895a45be","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","message":{"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeeF1KvTTvyw5uLJJawRM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WxRPU3Rck9Ffnb19GZNnWe","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://ai.google.dev/api/models","prompt":"What fields does the Gemini API models.list / GET /v1beta/models return per model? List exact field names (name, baseModelId, version, displayName, description, inputTokenLimit, outputTokenLimit, supportedGenerationMethods, temperature, topP, topK, maxTemperature, thinking). Does it include pricing or free-tier info?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1830,"cache_read_input_tokens":184643,"output_tokens":699,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":304},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1830},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":699,"cache_read_input_tokens":184643,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1830,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1830,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CeeF1JY7g2owNexGzmRDN","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"9cf500d1-3b00-43dc-8c1b-7f3d56904b46","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:46:45.230Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"9cf500d1-3b00-43dc-8c1b-7f3d56904b46","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"355cfc4f-9d72-4bb3-8805-f2dd57c05477","agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WxRPU3Rck9Ffnb19GZNnWe","type":"tool_result","content":"`models.list` returns a paginated wrapper containing `models[]` (each a `Model` resource) plus `nextPageToken`, described as \"A token, which can be sent as `pageToken` to retrieve the next page.\"\n\n**Per-model fields (from the Model resource JSON representation):**\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `name` | string | Resource name, format `models/{model}` |\n| `baseModelId` | string | \"The name of the base model, pass this to the generation request.\" |\n| `version` | string | Major version, e.g. `1.0` or `1.5` |\n| `displayName` | string | Human-readable, up to 128 characters |\n| `description` | string | \"A short description of the model.\" |\n| `inputTokenLimit` | integer | Max input tokens |\n| `outputTokenLimit` | integer | Max output tokens |\n| `supportedGenerationMethods[]` | string array | Pascal-case-ish method names like `generateContent`, `embedContent` |\n| `thinking` | boolean | \"Whether the model supports thinking.\" |\n| `temperature` | number | Backend default; range `[0.0,maxTemperature]` |\n| `maxTemperature` | number | \"The maximum temperature this model can use.\" |\n| `topP` | number | Default for nucleus sampling |\n| `topK` | integer | If empty, the model doesn't use top-k and it isn't an allowed generation parameter |\n\nThat's the complete set — all thirteen fields you listed are present, and there are no others.\n\n**Pricing / free tier: no.** Nothing in the Model resource covers cost, rate limits, quotas, or free-tier eligibility. The endpoint is scoped to \"supported functionality and context window sizing\" metadata only. You'd need Google's separate pricing documentation for billing details."}]},"uuid":"81addeaf-1c37-4754-a591-848742add992","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:46:58.781Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":112949,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"`models.list` returns a paginated wrapper containing `models[]` (each a `Model` resource) plus `nextPageToken`, described as \"A token, which can be sent as `pageToken` to retrieve the next page.\"\n\n**Per-model fields (from the Model resource JSON representation):**\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `name` | string | Resource name, format `models/{model}` |\n| `baseModelId` | string | \"The name of the base model, pass this to the generation request.\" |\n| `version` | string | Major version, e.g. `1.0` or `1.5` |\n| `displayName` | string | Human-readable, up to 128 characters |\n| `description` | string | \"A short description of the model.\" |\n| `inputTokenLimit` | integer | Max input tokens |\n| `outputTokenLimit` | integer | Max output tokens |\n| `supportedGenerationMethods[]` | string array | Pascal-case-ish method names like `generateContent`, `embedContent` |\n| `thinking` | boolean | \"Whether the model supports thinking.\" |\n| `temperature` | number | Backend default; range `[0.0,maxTemperature]` |\n| `maxTemperature` | number | \"The maximum temperature this model can use.\" |\n| `topP` | number | Default for nucleus sampling |\n| `topK` | integer | If empty, the model doesn't use top-k and it isn't an allowed generation parameter |\n\nThat's the complete set — all thirteen fields you listed are present, and there are no others.\n\n**Pricing / free tier: no.** Nothing in the Model resource covers cost, rate limits, quotas, or free-tier eligibility. The endpoint is scoped to \"supported functionality and context window sizing\" metadata only. You'd need Google's separate pricing documentation for billing details.","durationMs":9993,"url":"https://ai.google.dev/api/models"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9cf500d1-3b00-43dc-8c1b-7f3d56904b46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"5fbe22a3-d28e-4629-84fd-0979895a45be","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"355cfc4f-9d72-4bb3-8805-f2dd57c05477","agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E1hjbKpVo9J6SRboWhCAMN","type":"tool_result","content":"## Free model rate limits\n\nModels whose IDs end in `:free` are subject to platform-level request caps that depend on how many credits you've ever purchased:\n\n| Credits purchased (all time) | Requests/minute | Requests/day |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Under 10 | 20 | 50 |\n| 10 or more | 20 | 1,000 |\n\nSo the per-minute ceiling stays at 20 either way; buying at least 10 credits is what lifts the daily allowance from 50 to 1,000. Separately, Cloudflare DDoS protection will reject traffic that \"dramatically exceed[s] reasonable usage.\"\n\nA negative account balance can also trigger `402` errors even on free models — topping the balance back above zero restores access.\n\n## Handling 429s\n\nRate-limit rejections return a standard error body with `\"error_type\": \"rate_limit_exceeded\"`. These come either from OpenRouter's own limits or from the upstream provider (in which case `error.metadata.provider_code` may carry the provider's code, and fallback routing tries other providers first).\n\nNotably, successful responses carry no rate-limit headers — only OpenRouter's own 429 responses include `X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, and `X-RateLimit-Reset`, plus `Retry-After` when every provider returned a retry hint. Remedies: exponential backoff honoring `Retry-After`, purchasing credits or moving to the paid variant, or adding fallback models / loosening provider preferences.\n\nIf the limit is hit mid-stream, you get an SSE event with `finish_reason: \"error\"` rather than an HTTP 429, since the `200` header was already flushed.\n\n## The key endpoint\n\n`GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/key` (or `openRouter.apiKeys.getCurrent()` in the TypeScript SDK) returns a `data` object containing:\n\n- `label`\n- `limit`, `limit_reset`, `limit_remaining` — the optional per-key spending cap, its reset cadence, and what's left; `null` means unlimited\n- `include_byok_in_limit` — whether external BYOK usage counts toward that cap\n- `usage`, `usage_daily`, `usage_weekly`, `usage_monthly` — credits consumed all-time and per UTC day/week (Monday start)/month\n- `byok_usage` and its daily/weekly/monthly counterparts\n- `is_free_tier` — whether the account has ever paid for credits\n- a deprecated `rate_limit` object you can ignore\n\nPoll this endpoint to watch `limit_remaining` before requests start failing.\n\n## On the other variant suffixes\n\nThe source material here only documents `:free`. It doesn't describe `:nitro`, `:floor`, `:online`, `:extended`, or `:thinking`, and there's no `/api/v1/credits` endpoint mentioned — so I can't characterize those from this page. The docs index at `https://openrouter.ai/docs/llms.txt` would be the place to look for pages covering model variants.\n\nOne clarification worth noting: making extra accounts or API keys won't help, since capacity is governed globally — though different models carry different limits, so spreading load across models is a legitimate approach."}]},"uuid":"de7720df-10d7-4125-95df-4ed1b6c3b984","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:47:02.393Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":15859,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"## Free model rate limits\n\nModels whose IDs end in `:free` are subject to platform-level request caps that depend on how many credits you've ever purchased:\n\n| Credits purchased (all time) | Requests/minute | Requests/day |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Under 10 | 20 | 50 |\n| 10 or more | 20 | 1,000 |\n\nSo the per-minute ceiling stays at 20 either way; buying at least 10 credits is what lifts the daily allowance from 50 to 1,000. Separately, Cloudflare DDoS protection will reject traffic that \"dramatically exceed[s] reasonable usage.\"\n\nA negative account balance can also trigger `402` errors even on free models — topping the balance back above zero restores access.\n\n## Handling 429s\n\nRate-limit rejections return a standard error body with `\"error_type\": \"rate_limit_exceeded\"`. These come either from OpenRouter's own limits or from the upstream provider (in which case `error.metadata.provider_code` may carry the provider's code, and fallback routing tries other providers first).\n\nNotably, successful responses carry no rate-limit headers — only OpenRouter's own 429 responses include `X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, and `X-RateLimit-Reset`, plus `Retry-After` when every provider returned a retry hint. Remedies: exponential backoff honoring `Retry-After`, purchasing credits or moving to the paid variant, or adding fallback models / loosening provider preferences.\n\nIf the limit is hit mid-stream, you get an SSE event with `finish_reason: \"error\"` rather than an HTTP 429, since the `200` header was already flushed.\n\n## The key endpoint\n\n`GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/key` (or `openRouter.apiKeys.getCurrent()` in the TypeScript SDK) returns a `data` object containing:\n\n- `label`\n- `limit`, `limit_reset`, `limit_remaining` — the optional per-key spending cap, its reset cadence, and what's left; `null` means unlimited\n- `include_byok_in_limit` — whether external BYOK usage counts toward that cap\n- `usage`, `usage_daily`, `usage_weekly`, `usage_monthly` — credits consumed all-time and per UTC day/week (Monday start)/month\n- `byok_usage` and its daily/weekly/monthly counterparts\n- `is_free_tier` — whether the account has ever paid for credits\n- a deprecated `rate_limit` object you can ignore\n\nPoll this endpoint to watch `limit_remaining` before requests start failing.\n\n## On the other variant suffixes\n\nThe source material here only documents `:free`. It doesn't describe `:nitro`, `:floor`, `:online`, `:extended`, or `:thinking`, and there's no `/api/v1/credits` endpoint mentioned — so I can't characterize those from this page. The docs index at `https://openrouter.ai/docs/llms.txt` would be the place to look for pages covering model variants.\n\nOne clarification worth noting: making extra accounts or API keys won't help, since capacity is governed globally — though different models carry different limits, so spreading load across models is a legitimate approach.","durationMs":15457,"url":"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api-reference/limits"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5fbe22a3-d28e-4629-84fd-0979895a45be","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
