{"parentUuid":"fcc9d187-04fe-4772-948f-a4135a83781c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"355cfc4f-9d72-4bb3-8805-f2dd57c05477","agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GqwmSrSUzXsGq2Sy8Zu8e8","type":"tool_result","content":"REDIRECT DETECTED: The URL redirects to a location that was not fetched automatically.\n\nOriginal URL: https://docs.nebius.com/studio/inference/api\nRedirect URL (from the server's Location header — server-supplied, not verified): https://docs.tokenfactory.nebius.com/\nStatus: 307 Temporary Redirect\n\nTo complete your request, I need to fetch content from the redirected URL. Please use WebFetch again with these parameters:\n- url: \"https://docs.tokenfactory.nebius.com/\"\n- prompt: \"What does Nebius AI Studio's GET /v1/models return per model? Exact field names. Does it include pricing or free tier info? Also does Nebius have a free tier / trial credits?\""}]},"uuid":"e2f8210a-0dd3-47f6-a55c-5d190b77299a","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:47:39.204Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":658,"code":307,"codeText":"Temporary Redirect","result":"REDIRECT DETECTED: The URL redirects to a location that was not fetched automatically.\n\nOriginal URL: https://docs.nebius.com/studio/inference/api\nRedirect URL (from the server's Location header — server-supplied, not verified): https://docs.tokenfactory.nebius.com/\nStatus: 307 Temporary Redirect\n\nTo complete your request, I need to fetch content from the redirected URL. Please use WebFetch again with these parameters:\n- url: \"https://docs.tokenfactory.nebius.com/\"\n- prompt: \"What does Nebius AI Studio's GET /v1/models return per model? Exact field names. Does it include pricing or free tier info? Also does Nebius have a free tier / trial credits?\"","durationMs":2599,"url":"https://docs.nebius.com/studio/inference/api"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fcc9d187-04fe-4772-948f-a4135a83781c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"c71c7daa-6e63-4baa-94eb-ade2b10cb677","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"355cfc4f-9d72-4bb3-8805-f2dd57c05477","agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UoANjGDhtLicKa5UMLjjfT","type":"tool_result","content":"The page doesn't answer your question. The documented response schema stops at the envelope level and never expands the per-model object.\n\n**What's actually specified:**\n\n- The top-level return is an `object { errors, messages, result, success }`\n- `errors: array of unknown`\n- `messages: array of string`\n- `result: array of unknown`\n- `success: boolean`\n- A separate marketplace-format shape: `Data object { data }` with `data: array of unknown`, described as a \"Marketplace-format response\" pointing to OpenRouter's provider guide\n\nBecause `result` is typed as an array of unknown, none of the fields you listed — `id`, `source`, `name`, `description`, `task`, `created_at`, `tags`, or `properties` (with `property_id`/`value` pairs) — appear anywhere on this page. The 200 example is equally unhelpful: `\"result\"` contains a single empty object `{}`.\n\n**On pricing and context window:** nothing on this page mentions pricing, price, or context window in any form. There's no `properties` array documented, so there's no basis here for confirming which `property_id` values exist or what they carry.\n\n**Where the page does have detail** — the query parameters, which are fully enumerated: `author`, `format` (only accepts `\"openrouter\"`), `hide_experimental`, `include_deprecated` (\"include models for up to three months after their deprecation date\"), `page`, `per_page`, `search`, `source` (filter by Source Id), and `task`. Plus the path parameter `account_id`.\n\n**Suggested next steps:** the `format=openrouter` option routes to a documented external schema at openrouter.ai's provider guide, which does define pricing and context-length fields — that's a concrete lead. Otherwise, calling the endpoint directly against a real account is the fastest way to see the actual model object shape, or check Cloudflare's Workers AI model catalog docs rather than this API reference stub."}]},"uuid":"755e2b4c-9a14-4dbf-a02b-ff70fa69faef","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:47:46.589Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":2733,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The page doesn't answer your question. The documented response schema stops at the envelope level and never expands the per-model object.\n\n**What's actually specified:**\n\n- The top-level return is an `object { errors, messages, result, success }`\n- `errors: array of unknown`\n- `messages: array of string`\n- `result: array of unknown`\n- `success: boolean`\n- A separate marketplace-format shape: `Data object { data }` with `data: array of unknown`, described as a \"Marketplace-format response\" pointing to OpenRouter's provider guide\n\nBecause `result` is typed as an array of unknown, none of the fields you listed — `id`, `source`, `name`, `description`, `task`, `created_at`, `tags`, or `properties` (with `property_id`/`value` pairs) — appear anywhere on this page. The 200 example is equally unhelpful: `\"result\"` contains a single empty object `{}`.\n\n**On pricing and context window:** nothing on this page mentions pricing, price, or context window in any form. There's no `properties` array documented, so there's no basis here for confirming which `property_id` values exist or what they carry.\n\n**Where the page does have detail** — the query parameters, which are fully enumerated: `author`, `format` (only accepts `\"openrouter\"`), `hide_experimental`, `include_deprecated` (\"include models for up to three months after their deprecation date\"), `page`, `per_page`, `search`, `source` (filter by Source Id), and `task`. Plus the path parameter `account_id`.\n\n**Suggested next steps:** the `format=openrouter` option routes to a documented external schema at openrouter.ai's provider guide, which does define pricing and context-length fields — that's a concrete lead. Otherwise, calling the endpoint directly against a real account is the fastest way to see the actual model object shape, or check Cloudflare's Workers AI model catalog docs rather than this API reference stub.","durationMs":11999,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/api/resources/ai/subresources/models/methods/list/"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c71c7daa-6e63-4baa-94eb-ade2b10cb677","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
