{"parentUuid":"c087ee46-232b-4bd7-9cd8-38ad4ef34641","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","message":{"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeeF6b2CUKQikvJMr5c5j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015n16RYbuu4z7TGPBdepd1r","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/platform/pricing/","prompt":"Describe Cloudflare Workers AI pricing: the free daily Neuron allocation on the Workers Free plan, the Neurons concept, and whether per-model pricing is published in a machine-readable form. Give the exact free allocation numbers."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1499,"cache_read_input_tokens":190596,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1499,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CeeF6ZuiuDTyqMkMYmPW9","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f2301ad5-3a7b-4abd-b228-1ce537665db0","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:47:54.252Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"f2301ad5-3a7b-4abd-b228-1ce537665db0","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","message":{"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeeF6b2CUKQikvJMr5c5j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DbUz9MV72TyNZ3krgqh9Kj","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.tokenfactory.nebius.com/","prompt":"Does Nebius (Token Factory / AI Studio) GET /v1/models return pricing or free-tier info per model? What fields does it return? Does Nebius offer free trial credits or any free models?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1499,"cache_read_input_tokens":190596,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1499,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CeeF6ZuiuDTyqMkMYmPW9","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"cc413d52-cee6-451d-a083-241d91b0a2a4","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:47:54.957Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"f2301ad5-3a7b-4abd-b228-1ce537665db0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"355cfc4f-9d72-4bb3-8805-f2dd57c05477","agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015n16RYbuu4z7TGPBdepd1r","type":"tool_result","content":"**Free daily allocation:** Both the Workers Free and Workers Paid plans include \"10,000 Neurons per day at no charge.\" Going beyond that on the Free plan isn't possible — you'd need to upgrade, since the pricing table lists \"N/A - Upgrade to Workers Paid\" for Free-tier overage. On the Paid plan, additional usage costs $0.011 per 1,000 Neurons. Allocations reset each day at midnight UTC, and exceeding a limit causes subsequent operations to fail with an error.\n\n**What Neurons are:** Cloudflare describes them as \"our way of measuring AI outputs across different models, representing the GPU compute needed to perform your request.\" The idea is a serverless billing unit — you're charged for consumption rather than for provisioning or scaling GPU hardware yourself.\n\n**Machine-readable per-model pricing:** The page does publish extensive per-model rates, but only as human-readable HTML tables (LLM, embeddings, image, audio, and other categories), with each model shown in both dollar-denominated units and Neuron equivalents. The docs note that the token-price and Neuron-price columns are equivalent, displayed side by side so the two units can be compared easily.\n\nThe only structured data embedded on the page is a JSON-LD block, and it contains article metadata (headline, description, URL, publisher, date modified) — not pricing figures. There's a Markdown version of the page and an `llms.txt` documentation index referenced for discovery, but neither is described as a pricing API or a structured pricing feed. So: no, per-model pricing is not offered in a machine-readable format here.\n\nOne additional detail: certain models require a paid billing method regardless of the free allocation, including `@cf/moonshotai/kimi-k2.6`, `@cf/zai-org/glm-5.2`, and `@cf/deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-pro-0813`, among others. These can be accessed via the Workers Paid plan or prepaid AI Gateway credits."}]},"uuid":"b90b69c0-a0ee-454b-9189-f6d54ab92c9b","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:48:08.738Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":20576,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Free daily allocation:** Both the Workers Free and Workers Paid plans include \"10,000 Neurons per day at no charge.\" Going beyond that on the Free plan isn't possible — you'd need to upgrade, since the pricing table lists \"N/A - Upgrade to Workers Paid\" for Free-tier overage. On the Paid plan, additional usage costs $0.011 per 1,000 Neurons. Allocations reset each day at midnight UTC, and exceeding a limit causes subsequent operations to fail with an error.\n\n**What Neurons are:** Cloudflare describes them as \"our way of measuring AI outputs across different models, representing the GPU compute needed to perform your request.\" The idea is a serverless billing unit — you're charged for consumption rather than for provisioning or scaling GPU hardware yourself.\n\n**Machine-readable per-model pricing:** The page does publish extensive per-model rates, but only as human-readable HTML tables (LLM, embeddings, image, audio, and other categories), with each model shown in both dollar-denominated units and Neuron equivalents. The docs note that the token-price and Neuron-price columns are equivalent, displayed side by side so the two units can be compared easily.\n\nThe only structured data embedded on the page is a JSON-LD block, and it contains article metadata (headline, description, URL, publisher, date modified) — not pricing figures. There's a Markdown version of the page and an `llms.txt` documentation index referenced for discovery, but neither is described as a pricing API or a structured pricing feed. So: no, per-model pricing is not offered in a machine-readable format here.\n\nOne additional detail: certain models require a paid billing method regardless of the free allocation, including `@cf/moonshotai/kimi-k2.6`, `@cf/zai-org/glm-5.2`, and `@cf/deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-pro-0813`, among others. These can be accessed via the Workers Paid plan or prepaid AI Gateway credits.","durationMs":10533,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/platform/pricing/"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f2301ad5-3a7b-4abd-b228-1ce537665db0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"cc413d52-cee6-451d-a083-241d91b0a2a4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"355cfc4f-9d72-4bb3-8805-f2dd57c05477","agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DbUz9MV72TyNZ3krgqh9Kj","type":"tool_result","content":"The page above doesn't answer your questions. It's a quickstart that shows how to call the chat completions endpoint with the OpenAI SDK (Python, JavaScript, cURL) against `https://api.tokenfactory.nebius.com/v1/`, plus links to inference, integrations, fine-tuning, and API reference sections.\n\nSpecifically, nothing here covers:\n\n- **`GET /v1/models`** — the endpoint isn't mentioned at all, so I can't tell you which fields it returns or whether pricing/free-tier metadata is included.\n- **Pricing or free credits** — no mention of trial credits, promotional balances, or free models.\n\nWhat the content does confirm is that it's an \"OpenAI-compatible API,\" so a models listing endpoint would plausibly follow OpenAI's schema (id, object, created, owned_by), but that's inference on my part, not something stated here.\n\nTo get real answers, I'd check:\n\n1. The full documentation index the page points to: `https://docs.tokenfactory.nebius.com/llms.txt`, described as a way to \"discover all available pages before exploring further.\"\n2. The API reference linked as \"Learn how to authenticate and make requests to the inference API.\"\n3. The cookbook at `https://github.com/nebius/token-factory-cookbook`, which the page describes as containing \"solutions, examples and demo apps.\"\n4. Simply calling the endpoint yourself with your key and inspecting the JSON response — that's the fastest way to see the exact field set.\n\nFor account signup, the page notes you can register at tokenfactory.nebius.com and \"Log in using your Google or GitHub account,\" then obtain an API key — but it says nothing about what balance or credits an account starts with."}]},"uuid":"c58d4a24-ff5c-42b7-8d6e-08b51d378d35","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:48:09.550Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":3984,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The page above doesn't answer your questions. It's a quickstart that shows how to call the chat completions endpoint with the OpenAI SDK (Python, JavaScript, cURL) against `https://api.tokenfactory.nebius.com/v1/`, plus links to inference, integrations, fine-tuning, and API reference sections.\n\nSpecifically, nothing here covers:\n\n- **`GET /v1/models`** — the endpoint isn't mentioned at all, so I can't tell you which fields it returns or whether pricing/free-tier metadata is included.\n- **Pricing or free credits** — no mention of trial credits, promotional balances, or free models.\n\nWhat the content does confirm is that it's an \"OpenAI-compatible API,\" so a models listing endpoint would plausibly follow OpenAI's schema (id, object, created, owned_by), but that's inference on my part, not something stated here.\n\nTo get real answers, I'd check:\n\n1. The full documentation index the page points to: `https://docs.tokenfactory.nebius.com/llms.txt`, described as a way to \"discover all available pages before exploring further.\"\n2. The API reference linked as \"Learn how to authenticate and make requests to the inference API.\"\n3. The cookbook at `https://github.com/nebius/token-factory-cookbook`, which the page describes as containing \"solutions, examples and demo apps.\"\n4. Simply calling the endpoint yourself with your key and inspecting the JSON response — that's the fastest way to see the exact field set.\n\nFor account signup, the page notes you can register at tokenfactory.nebius.com and \"Log in using your Google or GitHub account,\" then obtain an API key — but it says nothing about what balance or credits an account starts with.","durationMs":9642,"url":"https://docs.tokenfactory.nebius.com/"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cc413d52-cee6-451d-a083-241d91b0a2a4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
