": \"chat\",\r\n \"output_cost_per_token\": 2.49998e-06,\r\n \"output_dbu_cost_per_token\": 3.5714e-05,\r\n \"source\": \"https://www.databricks.com/product/pricing/proprietary-foundation-model-serving\",\r\n \"supports_function_calling\": true,\r\n \"supports_prompt_caching\": true,\r\n \"supports_tool_choice\": true\r\n}\r\n\r\nzero-cost entries: 130 ['sample_spec', 'amazon.rerank-v1:0', 'anthropic.claude-mythos-preview', 'azure_ai/cohere-rerank-v3-english', 'azure_ai/cohere-rerank-v3-multilingual', 'azure_ai/cohere-rerank-v3.5', 'azure_ai/cohere-rerank-v4.0-pro', 'azure_ai/cohere-rerank-v4.0-fast', 'cloudflare/@cf/google/gemma-2b-it-lora', 'cloudflare/@cf/mistral/mistral-7b-instruct-v0.2-lora']","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0bc246f8-1ec2-41f5-9da6-a85209b8be0f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"05c74aad-ec8f-4ee6-bb20-5bb8386af78a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","message":{"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeeFBmeoQ94puYowzcz35","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3776,"cache_read_input_tokens":196530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3776,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CeeFBjseJwzjkfGh1Qccd","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1b44a736-8ed5-4593-9803-2a84a6d0421f","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:49:03.059Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"1b44a736-8ed5-4593-9803-2a84a6d0421f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","message":{"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeeFBmeoQ94puYowzcz35","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough evidence. Here are the findings.\n\n---\n\n# Free/Paid Determinability Across LLM Provider Catalogues\n\n**Method:** I read `C:\\Users\\osami\\.llmkeys\\providers.json` and `registry.json` (read-only; no key values touched — neither file stores secrets anyway, only `headersTemplate` patterns and `envVarName` references). I then made **unauthenticated** `GET` probes to public `/v1/models` endpoints and fetched public API docs. No authenticated calls, no billed calls. Where an endpoint returned 401/403 I stopped and fell back to documentation, and I say so explicitly below.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What `/v1/models` actually returns — live-probed evidence\n\nI probed 16 endpoints unauthenticated. Seven returned **200 with full catalogues**; the rest returned 401/403 and were not retried with credentials.\n\n| Provider | Unauth status | Models | Pricing in response? | Free-signal field |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **OpenRouter** | 200 (fully public) | 421 | **Yes** — `pricing.prompt` / `pricing.completion` as decimal strings | `\"0\"` + `:free` id suffix |\n| **Hugging Face router** | 200 (public) | 136 (314 model-provider rows) | Partial — `providers[].pricing.{input,output}` present on only 208/314 rows | **explicit `providers[].is_free` boolean** on all 314 rows |\n| **Novita** | 200 (public) | 154 | **Yes** — `input_token_price_per_m`, `output_token_price_per_m` (int, 1e-4 USD/M) + nested `pricing.prompt.{origin_price_per_m, price_per_m, price_per_m_decimal}` | price `0` (unreliable, see §3) |\n| **Venice AI** | 200 (public) | 112 | **Yes** — `model_spec.pricing.{input,cache_input,output}.{usd,diem}` | none zero-priced |\n| **Chutes** | 200 (public) | 14 | **Yes** — `pricing.{prompt,completion,input_cache_read}` USD/M **and** `price.{input,output}.{tao,usd}` | none zero-priced |\n| **Pollinations** | 200 (public) | 362 | **Yes but in \"pollen\"** — `pricing.currency: \"pollen\"`, `promptTextTokens`, `completionTextTokens` | none zero; `per_user_rpm` on 210 models |\n| **LLM7** | 200 (public) | 44 | **Yes** — `pricing.{input,output,cached_input,currency,unit}`, `pricing_mode` ∈ {token, second, image} | `tier` ∈ {pro, turbo} — **no `free` value exists**; none zero-priced |\n| **AionLabs** | 200 (public) | 4 | **Yes** — `pricing.{prompt,completion,input_cache_read}` | none zero-priced |\n| **NVIDIA NIM** | 200 (public) | 82 | **No** — only `id`, `object`, `created`, `owned_by` | **none** |\n| **SambaNova** | 200 (public, partial) | 7 only | **Yes** — `pricing.{prompt,completion}` USD/token strings, `context_length`, `max_completion_tokens` | none zero (but list is a public subset — `providers.json` `testModel` names a model not in the unauth 7) |\n| DeepSeek / Groq / Together / Fireworks / Mistral / Nebius / Hyperbolic | 401 | — | see docs below | — |\n| Cerebras | 403 | — | **No** (docs: id/object/created/owned_by only) | none |\n| Google Gemini | 403 | — | **No** | none |\n\n**Documentation-sourced (auth required, not probed):**\n\n- **Groq** — `id`, `object`, `created`, `owned_by`, `active`, `context_window`, `public_apps`, `max_completion_tokens`. **No pricing, no tier.**\n- **DeepSeek** — `id`, `object`, `owned_by`. Nothing else. Docs explicitly redirect to a separate pricing page.\n- **Together AI** — **has pricing.** `ModelInfo`: `id`, `object`, `created`, `type` (chat/language/code/image/embedding/moderation/rerank), `display_name`, `organization`, `link`, `license`, `context_length`, `pricing{hourly, input, output, base, finetune, cached_input?}`. Query param `dedicated` changes the result set.\n- **Fireworks** — the rich data is on the **control-plane** `GET /v1/accounts/{account_id}/models`, not the OpenAI-compat path: `contextLength`, `trainingContextLength`, `supportsImageInput`, `supportsTools`, `supportsServerless`, `state` (UPLOADING/READY), **`deprecationDate`**, and pricing nested under `serverlessModes[].skuInfos` (`sku`, `amount`, `unit: \"1M tokens\"`) — marked read-only and \"computed live at read time\".\n- **Mistral** — `BaseModelCard`: `id`, `object`, `created`, `owned_by`, `capabilities{completion_chat, completion_fim, function_calling, fine_tuning, vision, classification}`, `name`, `description`, `max_context_length`, `aliases`, **`deprecation` (date-time)**, **`deprecation_replacement_model`**, `default_model_temperature`, `internal`, `type`. **No pricing.**\n- **Google Gemini** (native `v1beta/models`) — `name`, `baseModelId`, `version`, `displayName`, `description`, `inputTokenLimit`, `outputTokenLimit`, `supportedGenerationMethods[]`, `thinking`, `temperature`, `maxTemperature`, `topP`, `topK`. **No pricing, no quota, no free-tier flag.** The OpenAI-compat layer your `providers.json` uses (`/v1beta/openai/models`) returns strictly less.\n- **Cloudflare Workers AI** — `/v1/models` is **not supported (405)**, confirmed by your own note. Native `GET /accounts/{id}/ai/models/search` supports `include_deprecated`, `hide_experimental`, `task`, `author`, and notably **`format=openrouter`**, which returns an OpenRouter-schema marketplace payload (i.e. with pricing fields). Cloudflare's own API reference types `result` as `array of unknown` — useless as a schema source.\n- **Nebius, Hyperbolic, Alibaba DashScope compatible-mode** — **I could not confirm.** All returned 401, and I did not find a doc page specifying the per-model response schema. I am leaving these blank rather than guessing.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OpenRouter schema (the richest case) — verified against a live 421-model response\n\nTop level: `{ data: [...], total_count, links }`.\n\nPer-model fields, all 421/421 present:\n\n```\nid, canonical_slug, hugging_face_id, name, created, description,\ncontext_length, architecture, pricing, top_provider, per_request_limits,\nsupported_parameters, default_parameters, supported_voices,\nknowledge_cutoff, expiration_date, links\n```\n\nPlus optional: `reasoning` (294/421), `benchmarks` (240/421), `alias_target` (13/421).\n\n**`pricing`** — values are **decimal strings in USD per token**, not per million:\n\n| Subfield | Present on |\n|---|---|\n| `prompt` | 421 |\n| `completion` | 421 |\n| `input_cache_read` | 254 |\n| `web_search` | 151 |\n| `input_cache_write` | 75 |\n| `overrides` | 60 |\n| `audio` | 32 |\n| `input_cache_write_1h` | 31 |\n| `internal_reasoning` | 30 |\n| `image` | 29 |\n| `input_audio_cache` | 27 |\n| `image_output` | 9 |\n| `audio_output` | 2 |\n\nNote `request` and `per_request_limits` are documented but **`per_request_limits` was `null` on all 421 models** and no `request` key appeared — do not depend on either.\n\n**`architecture`** (421/421): `modality` (e.g. `\"text+image+video->text\"`), `input_modalities[]`, `output_modalities[]`, `tokenizer`, `instruct_type`.\n\n**`top_provider`** (421/421): `context_length`, `max_completion_tokens`, `is_moderated`.\n\n**A free model looks exactly like this** (real record):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it:free\",\n  \"canonical_slug\": \"google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it-20260403\",\n  \"name\": \"Google: Gemma 4 26B A4B  (free)\",\n  \"context_length\": 262144,\n  \"pricing\": { \"prompt\": \"0\", \"completion\": \"0\" },\n  \"top_provider\": { \"context_length\": 262144, \"max_completion_tokens\": 32768, \"is_moderated\": false },\n  \"per_request_limits\": null\n}\n```\n\nNote the free variant's `pricing` object collapses to **only** `prompt` and `completion` — no cache/image/reasoning keys. That absence is itself a weak secondary signal.\n\n**Sub-resource with per-endpoint pricing:** `GET /api/v1/models/{canonical_slug}/endpoints` returns `endpoints[]` with `provider_name`, `tag`, `quantization`, `context_length`, `max_completion_tokens`, `max_prompt_tokens`, `pricing.{prompt,completion,discount}`, `status`, `uptime_last_30m/5m/1d`, `supports_tool_choice`, `supports_implicit_caching`. Useful if you ever need \"which upstream actually serves this\".\n\n**Account-level free signal:** `GET /api/v1/key` returns `is_free_tier` (has the account ever paid), plus `limit`, `limit_remaining`, `usage`, `usage_daily/weekly/monthly`. That is **account** free-ness, not model free-ness. Requires auth.\n\n**`:free` rate limits (documented):** 20 req/min regardless; 50 req/day under 10 lifetime credits purchased, 1,000 req/day at ≥10. Successful responses carry **no** rate-limit headers — `X-RateLimit-Limit/Remaining/Reset` appear only on OpenRouter's own 429s.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Naming conventions — how reliable is the suffix?\n\n**OpenRouter, measured on the live catalogue:**\n\n- 421 models, 21 with `pricing.prompt == \"0\" && pricing.completion == \"0\"`, 18 with `:free` suffix.\n- **`:free` → zero-priced: 18/18. Precision = 100%.**\n- **zero-priced → `:free`: 18/21. Recall = 86%.** The three misses: `openrouter/free` (the \"Free Models Router\" meta-model), `google/lyria-3-pro-preview`, `google/lyria-3-clip-preview` (audio-output previews, temporarily unpriced).\n\nSo on OpenRouter the suffix **never lies positively**, but **misses free models**. Never infer \"not free\" from suffix absence.\n\nThe suffix namespace is generic, not free-specific: the live catalogue also carries **66 `:batch`-suffixed** models. Whatever parser you write must treat `:free` as one value in a variant enum.\n\n**Where the convention breaks — a concrete counter-example.** Pollinations carries community-published re-exports whose ids keep the upstream suffix but whose Pollinations pricing does not:\n\n| Pollinations id | `pricing` |\n|---|---|\n| `AkshayCoder48/meituan-longcat-2.0-free` | `promptTextTokens: 0.0000003`, `completionTextTokens: 0.0000012` — **non-zero** |\n| `AkshayCoder48/free-clips` | `promptTextTokens: 0.00000003` — **non-zero** |\n| `YoannDev90/poolside-laguna-s-2.1:free` | `{ currency: \"pollen\" }` — **no price fields at all** (unknown, not zero) |\n| `vendouple/laguna-s-2.1:free` | `{ currency: \"pollen\" }` + `per_user_rpm: 5` |\n\nThat is the case your rule was written for: suffix present, price non-zero or absent → **leave blank**.\n\n**Suffix usage per your own `providers.json` notes** (empirically probed, dated 2026-08):\n\n| Convention | Providers |\n|---|---|\n| `:free` | openrouter, kilo (13 of 362), tokenharbor, nousresearch (solar-pro4, laguna-s/xs-2.1, hy3, step-3.7-flash, longcat-2.0), zenmux |\n| `-free` | tokenrouter, teamorouter, nararouter, opencode (partial), aihubmix, zenmux (`z-ai/glm-5.3-free`) |\n| `/free` | orcarouter (`orcarouter/free`), kilo (`kilo-auto/free`, `openrouter/free`) |\n| **No suffix, free anyway** | opencode's `big-pickle`; gmicloud (uses an `is_free` flag instead); agnes (whole platform currently free) |\n| **Suffix, but not really free** | routllm — your note says there are *no* free-suffixed models; \"free\" there means the **account plan**, gated by a per-model `tier_required` field (0 = free plan, 1 = paid) |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Other reliable signals\n\n**Explicit boolean flags (strongest):**\n- **Hugging Face** — `providers[].is_free`. Exists on every one of 314 model-provider rows. Currently **0 are `true`** (matches your note: \"no truly free-tier models found via is_free flag\"). It rotates, so re-fetch. Caveat: 106/314 rows carry **no `pricing` dict at all** (e.g. `fireworks-ai`, `zai-org` rows), so `is_free: false` there is asserted without a price to back it.\n- **GMICloud** — your note records `GET /v1/models` returns an **`is_free` flag per model**, confirmed free: `MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3`, `MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M2.7`, with a real chat probe passing 2026-08-26. I could not re-verify (auth required) but this is your own empirical record.\n- **RoutLLM** — `tier_required` integer per model (0 = reachable on the free account plan).\n\n**Published machine-readable pricing catalogues (third-party — this is the big one for your gaps):**\n\n- **`https://models.dev/api.json`** — 4.4 MB, **212 providers, 7,502 models**, no auth. Per-model: `cost.{input,output}`, `limit.{context,output}`, `modalities.{input,output}`, `release_date`, `last_updated`, `reasoning`, `tool_call`, `structured_output`, `attachment`, `temperature`, `open_weights`, `family`.\n  **Covers 27 of your 47 providers**, including exotic ones nothing else indexes: `gmicloud`, `zenmux`, `tokenrouter`, `orcarouter`, `opencode`, `agnes`, `kilo`, `agentrouter`, `aihubmix`, `chutes`, `venice`, `cloudflare-workers-ai`, `ollama-cloud`.\n  **Does not cover (20):** indeedwebid, seekai, routllm, teamorouter, fanar, pollinations, nararouter, tokenharbor, githubcopilot, llm7, aionlabs, **sambanova**, nscale, tabiai, bai, commandcode, gorouter, bluesminds, youcom, nousresearch.\n  Zero-cost counts it reports: openrouter 21 (exactly matches my live probe — good calibration), opencode 30, kilo 24, orcarouter 5, zenmux 7, aihubmix 4, agnes 2, bigmodel 2, google 2.\n  **Two failure modes to guard against:** (a) `nvidia` shows **99 of 103 models at cost 0**, which encodes \"free to try on build.nvidia.com with credits\", not a $0 token price — semantically different from OpenRouter's `\"0\"`; (b) `ollama` has **22/22 with no `cost` field at all** — correctly modelling \"unknown\", which your schema should propagate as blank rather than coerce to 0.\n\n- **`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/main/model_prices_and_context_window.json`** — 2.1 MB, 3,518 entries, 131 `litellm_provider` values, no auth. Per-entry: `input_cost_per_token`, `output_cost_per_token`, `cache_read_input_token_cost`, `cache_creation_input_token_cost`, `max_input_tokens`, `max_output_tokens`, `mode`, `supports_function_calling`, `supports_vision`, `supports_prompt_caching`, `supports_tool_choice`, and a `source` URL citing the vendor pricing page. Covers `dashscope`, `hyperbolic`, `cerebras`, `cloudflare`, `github_copilot`, `gmi`, `fireworks_ai`, `deepinfra`.\n  **Critical caveat: LiteLLM's `0` mostly means \"not populated\", not \"free.\"** Of its 130 zero-cost entries, most are rerank/embedding/LoRA models billed per-request. **Do not treat a LiteLLM 0 as evidence of free-ness.**\n\n**Rate-limit / quota signals:**\n- **Pollinations** — `per_user_rpm` on 210/362 models. Presence of an RPM quota implies a free allowance exists, but tells you nothing about price.\n- **Cloudflare Workers AI** — **10,000 Neurons/day free** on both Workers Free and Paid plans, reset at midnight UTC. But per-model pricing is published **only as HTML tables**, and specific models (`@cf/moonshotai/kimi-k2.6`, `@cf/zai-org/glm-5.2`, `@cf/deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-pro-0813`) **require paid billing regardless of the free allocation** — so \"Cloudflare has a free tier\" does not make any given Cloudflare model free.\n- **OpenRouter** — rate-limit headers appear only on 429 responses, so they cannot be used as a passive discovery signal.\n\n**Deprecation / availability signals:**\n- **AionLabs** — `expires_at` + `replacement_model_id` per model.\n- **Mistral** — `deprecation` (ISO datetime) + `deprecation_replacement_model`.\n- **Fireworks** — `deprecationDate` (structured y/m/d) + `state`.\n- **Novita** — `status` field, values `1` and `4`; `4` correlates with retired models (llama-3-8b-instruct, glm-4.5, deepseek-v3-0324, qwen2.5-*).\n- **OpenRouter** — `expiration_date` (non-null on only 10/421), `knowledge_cutoff` (183/421), `alias_target` on 13 `~vendor/model-latest` pointers.\n- **Cloudflare** — `include_deprecated` query flag, \"up to three months after their deprecation date\".\n\n---\n\n## 5. What is genuinely NOT determinable without a billed call\n\n**Category A — no programmatic signal exists at all. Always leave the free field blank.**\n\n| Provider | Why |\n|---|---|\n| **NVIDIA NIM** | `/v1/models` returns only `id`/`object`/`created`/`owned_by` across all 82 models. Verified live. models.dev's 99-of-103 \"cost 0\" is a credits-grant claim, not a token price — do not import it. |\n| **Cerebras** | Same four fields. No pricing anywhere in the API. |\n| **Google Gemini** | Neither the native nor the OpenAI-compat models endpoint carries price, quota, or tier. Google's free tier is per-key and per-model rate limits published only in HTML docs. |\n| **DeepSeek** | Three fields. Docs explicitly punt to a separate pricing page. |\n| **Groq** | No pricing, no tier. Free-ness is an account-level rate-limit state invisible to the API. |\n| **GitHub Copilot** | Your note is decisive: no public chat-completions REST endpoint at all. There is no models endpoint to query. |\n| **Alibaba / DashScope** | I could not verify the compatible-mode `/v1/models` schema (401, no doc page found). Additionally your workspace uses a **per-workspace domain** — the schema may not generalize. Leave blank. |\n| **Nebius, Hyperbolic** | 401; no doc page specifying the model-object schema found. I will not guess. |\n\n**Category B — a catalogue exists but is a *proven liar* about what you can actually call. Blank unless separately probed.**\n\nYour own live probes already documented this and it is the strongest argument for the leave-empty rule:\n\n- **b.ai** — catalogue lists 42 models including Claude Opus 5 / GPT-5.6 / Gemini 3.1 Pro; **only 7 actually return 200** on a zero-balance key. The other 35 return `403 access_denied \"Deposit required to unlock premium models\"`. A catalogue listing is not an entitlement.\n- **commandcode** — all 58 listed models, on both endpoints, return `400 insufficient credits`. Nothing is callable.\n- **Venice AI** — `/v1/models` returns 200 with full pricing, but `POST /chat/completions` returns `400 Insufficient USD or Diem balance`. Catalogue reachable, inference not.\n- **indeedwebid** — models list 200s; every chat call 502s.\n- **Novita** — of 11 zero-priced models, `ai_infer_test_1/2/3`, `dev/glm46`, `bunny`, `gt-4p` are plainly internal/staging entries, and two more are `status: 4`. Zero price here means \"unpriced internal\", not \"free to you\".\n- **opencode / chutes / aihubmix** — `requiresBalance: true`; paid models fail with quota errors until recharged.\n\n**Category C — the ambiguity that no field can resolve.** \"Free\" is at least four different things, and every provider conflates them:\n\n1. **$0 token price** (OpenRouter `:free`, gmicloud `is_free`) — the only kind actually machine-readable.\n2. **Free account plan gating a model subset** (routllm `tier_required`, OpenRouter `is_free_tier`, HF monthly credit allowance) — model is priced, but your plan covers it.\n3. **Free daily quota in a non-USD unit** (Cloudflare Neurons, Pollinations pollen, Ollama Cloud daily allowance) — priced, but the first N are free.\n4. **Time-limited promo** (opencode's \"limited-time promo\" free list, agnes \"currently free\") — true today, false next month, with no expiry field anywhere.\n\nNothing in any `/v1/models` response distinguishes 1 from 2, 3, or 4. If your catalogue's `free` column means \"costs me $0 per token\", only signal type 1 can populate it.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Per-model metadata beyond free/paid, by provider\n\n| Field | Reliably available from |\n|---|---|\n| **Context window** | OpenRouter (`context_length` + `top_provider.context_length`), Together (`context_length`), Groq (`context_window`), Mistral (`max_context_length`), Gemini (`inputTokenLimit`), Fireworks (`contextLength`), Novita (`context_size`), Venice (`context_length` + `model_spec.availableContextTokens`), Chutes (`context_length`/`max_model_len`), SambaNova (`context_length`), LLM7 (`context_window.tokens`), AionLabs (`context_length`), HF (`providers[].context_length`), Pollinations (166/362) |\n| **Max output tokens** | OpenRouter (`top_provider.max_completion_tokens`), Groq (`max_completion_tokens`, retrieve endpoint), Gemini (`outputTokenLimit`), Novita (`max_output_tokens`), Venice (`model_spec.maxCompletionTokens`), SambaNova, Chutes (`max_output_length`), AionLabs |\n| **Modality** | OpenRouter (`architecture.modality` + `input_modalities[]`/`output_modalities[]`), HF (`architecture.input_modalities`/`output_modalities`), Novita, Chutes, Pollinations (`input_modalities`/`output_modalities`), Venice (`capabilities.supportsVision/AudioInput/VideoInput`), LLM7 (`modalities`), Mistral (`capabilities.vision`), Fireworks (`supportsImageInput`) |\n| **Created / release date** | OpenRouter (`created`, Unix), Together (`created`), Groq, Mistral, Novita, Venice, Chutes, HF, Pollinations, NVIDIA (present but values look unreliable), Cerebras (docs show `created: 0` in examples — **do not trust**), AionLabs (`date`, ISO) |\n| **Deprecation** | Mistral (`deprecation` + `deprecation_replacement_model`), AionLabs (`expires_at` + `replacement_model_id`), Fireworks (`deprecationDate` + `state`), Cloudflare (`include_deprecated` filter), Novita (`status: 4` — inferred, not documented), OpenRouter (`expiration_date`, but only 10/421 populated) |\n| **Availability / uptime** | OpenRouter `/models/{slug}/endpoints` (`uptime_last_30m/5m/1d`, `status`), LLM7 (`availability_last_hour_percent`), HF (`providers[].status: \"live\"`, `first_token_latency_ms`, `throughput`), Venice (`model_spec.offline`) |\n| **Tool / structured-output support** | OpenRouter (`supported_parameters[]`), HF (`supports_tools`, `supports_structured_output`), Novita (`features[]`), Chutes (`supported_features[]`), Venice (`capabilities.supportsFunctionCalling`), Mistral (`capabilities.function_calling`), Fireworks (`supportsTools`), LLM7 (`tools_calling`) |\n| **Reasoning** | OpenRouter (`reasoning.{mandatory, default_enabled}` on 294/421 — **directly actionable**, your `providers.json` notes that mandatory-reasoning models return empty content unless `max_tokens ≥ 512`), Novita (`features` includes `reasoning`), Venice, LLM7, AionLabs |\n| **Benchmarks** | OpenRouter only (`benchmarks.artificial_analysis.{intelligence_index, coding_index, agentic_index}` on 240/421) |\n\n---\n\n## 7. What `providers.json` already gives you\n\n`C:\\Users\\osami\\.llmkeys\\providers.json` — a JSON **array of 47 provider objects**. No secrets stored; `headersTemplate` holds a `{key}` placeholder pattern only.\n\nFields, with population counts:\n\n| Field | Present | Content |\n|---|---|---|\n| `provider` | 47/47 | slug |\n| `baseUrl` | 47/47 | inference base (empty for githubcopilot) — **you must append `/models` yourself; there is no dedicated models-endpoint field** |\n| `protocol` | 47/47 | `openai` (44), `anthropic` (1), `generic` (2) |\n| `headersTemplate` | 47/47 | auth pattern |\n| `testModel` | 47/47 | one known-callable id per provider (empty for githubcopilot/youcom) |\n| `docsUrl` | 47/47 | |\n| `notes` | 47/47 | **prose, often carrying the free-tier answer** |\n| `requiresBalance` | 47/47 | boolean — **13 true** |\n| `updated` | 47/47 | ISO timestamp |\n| `maxTokensParam` | 30/47 | `max_tokens` vs `max_completion_tokens` |\n| `accountInfo` | 29/47 | workspace/account ids, console URLs, some free-credit notes |\n\n**What you already have that bears on free/paid:**\n\n- `requiresBalance: true` on 13 providers (seekai, zenmux, routllm, tokenrouter, teamorouter, pollinations, opencode, cerebras, sambanova, chutes, bai, commandcode, gorouter, veniceai, aihubmix, xai). This is a **provider-level** gate, not per-model, but it is a hard \"nothing here is free without money\" for several of them.\n- `notes` already encodes, in prose, the free-model list for ~15 providers — e.g. opencode's seven promo models named explicitly, zenmux's \"7 genuinely $0 models\", gmicloud's `is_free` flag and confirmed free ids, kilo's \"13 `:free`-suffixed\", tokenharbor/tokenrouter/nararouter \"`-free` suffixed ids are genuinely free\", b.ai's 7-of-42 probe result.\n- `accountInfo.freeCredits` exists on exactly one provider (youcom: \"$100 complimentary\"), and `accountInfo.balanceNote` on one (aihubmix).\n\n**What is missing and must be fetched or added:**\n\n1. **No models-endpoint URL field.** Almost always `baseUrl + \"/models\"`, but there are at least three exceptions your notes flag: Cloudflare (`/v1/models` → 405, needs native `/ai/models/search`), Kilo (`baseUrl` has no `/v1`, path is `/api/gateway/chat/completions`), AionLabs (response key is `models`, **not** `data`). Add an explicit `modelsUrl` + `modelsResponseKey`.\n2. **No structured free/paid field.** Everything is prose in `notes`. Nothing machine-readable.\n3. **No pricing hints, no per-model records at all.** The file is provider-scoped; there is no model table.\n4. **No free-signal-kind discriminator** — nothing distinguishes \"has an `is_free` flag\" (gmicloud, HF) from \"use `:free` suffix\" (openrouter, kilo) from \"no signal\" (nvidia, cerebras).\n\n`registry.json` (56 entries: `id`, `provider`, `bucket`, `tier`, `envVarName`, `notes`, `added`) has a `tier` field — but it is `free`(42) / `paid`(13) / `management`(1) describing **the credential's account plan**, not model pricing. Your own routllm note makes the distinction explicit: *\"'free' key tier means free ACCOUNT plan\"*. Do not let `registry.tier` leak into a model-level free column.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Recommended per-provider capability table\n\nReliability legend: **A** = authoritative machine-readable price on the model object · **B** = explicit boolean/tier flag · **C** = naming convention only · **D** = prose/manual only · **✗** = no signal, leave blank.\n\n| Provider | Signal | Field(s) | Reliability | Populate `free`? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| openrouter | price + suffix | `pricing.prompt/completion == \"0\"`; `:free` | **A** | Yes — use price, not suffix |\n| gmicloudai | explicit flag | `is_free` per model | **B** | Yes |\n| huggingface | explicit flag + partial price | `providers[].is_free`, `providers[].pricing` | **B** (106/314 rows lack price) | Yes, but per-provider-row not per-model |\n| together | price | `pricing.{input,output,base,hourly}` | **A** (auth) | Yes |\n| novita | price | `input_token_price_per_m`/`output_token_price_per_m` | **A**, but 0 ⇒ often internal/`status:4` | Yes **only if** `status == 1` and id is not a test/dev entry |\n| venice | price | `model_spec.pricing.input.usd` | **A** | Yes (currently: none free) |\n| chutes | price | `pricing.prompt/completion` + `price.*.usd` | **A** | Yes (currently: none free) |\n| aionlabs | price | `pricing.prompt/completion` | **A** (`models` key, not `data`) | Yes |\n| llm7 | price + tier | `pricing.input`, `tier` | **A** (no `free` tier value exists) | Yes → all paid |\n| sambanova | price | `pricing.prompt/completion` | **A**, but unauth list is a 7-model subset | Yes, for listed models only |\n| pollinations | pollen price | `pricing.currency: \"pollen\"` | **C/✗** — non-USD; suffixed ids demonstrably not free | **Leave blank** |\n| routllm | tier gate | `tier_required` (0/1) | **B** — plan gate, not price | Blank for price; record as plan-gated |\n| zenmux | suffix + models.dev | `-free`; models.dev 7 zero-cost | **C** | Yes if cross-checked |\n| kilo | suffix + models.dev | `:free`, `/free`; models.dev 24 zero-cost | **C** | Yes if cross-checked |\n| orcarouter | suffix + models.dev | `/free`, `-free`; models.dev 5 zero-cost | **C** | Yes if cross-checked |\n| opencode | prose + models.dev | 7 named promo models; models.dev 30 zero-cost | **D** — time-limited promo | Yes with a `verified_at` stamp |\n| tokenrouter / nararouter / teamorouter / tokenharbor | suffix only | `-free` / `:free` | **C** — your probes back it, no price field | Yes, but flag low confidence |\n| aihubmix | suffix + prose | `*-free`; `requiresBalance` for the rest | **C/D** | Yes for `-free` only |\n| nousresearch | suffix | `:free` (6 named in `accountInfo.freeModels`) | **C** | Yes |\n| agnes | prose | \"currently free\" platform-wide | **D** | Yes with expiry caveat |\n| cloudflare | quota, not price | 10k Neurons/day; some models paid-only | **D** — HTML tables only | **Leave blank** |\n| ollama (cloud) | quota | \"free daily allowance\" | **D**; models.dev has 22/22 `cost` absent | **Leave blank** |\n| groq | ✗ | — | **✗** | **Blank** |\n| deepseek | ✗ | — | **✗** | **Blank** |\n| nvidia | ✗ | — | **✗** (ignore models.dev's 99 zeros) | **Blank** |\n| cerebras | ✗ | — | **✗** | **Blank** |\n| google | ✗ | — | **✗** | **Blank** |\n| mistral | ✗ (rich metadata, no price) | — | **✗** | **Blank** |\n| openai / anthropic / xai / cohere / bigmodel / alibaba / nscale / fanar / bluesminds / seekai / indeedwebid / llm7 | ✗ or all-paid | — | **✗** | **Blank** (or `No` only where you have a live probe) |\n| githubcopilot / youcom | not an LLM chat API | — | n/a | **Blank / exclude** |\n| tabiai / gorouter | ✗ + cost hazard | 4 Opus-only models, no pricing fields | **✗** — and your notes warn a test call is *not* cheap | **Blank; do not probe** |\n| bai / commandcode | catalogue lies | listing ≠ entitlement (probed) | **✗** | **Blank** |\n\n---\n\n## Bottom line\n\n- **Only three providers give you a first-party, per-model, machine-readable answer:** OpenRouter (`pricing.prompt`/`completion` as `\"0\"`), Hugging Face (`providers[].is_free`), and GMICloud (`is_free`). Together, Novita, Venice, Chutes, SambaNova, LLM7 and AionLabs give you real prices, which answers free/paid by arithmetic — but none of them currently expose a single $0 model except Novita, whose zeros are mostly internal entries.\n- **`:free` is safe as a positive signal, unsafe as a negative one, and unsafe across providers.** On OpenRouter its precision is 100% and recall 86%. On Pollinations it is demonstrably wrong. Never use it alone outside a provider you have probed.\n- **`models.dev/api.json` is your best gap-filler** — 212 providers, no auth, covers 27 of your 47 including the exotic routers nothing else indexes. But its `cost: 0` for NVIDIA encodes \"free credits\", not \"$0/token\", so import it as a *hint requiring confirmation*, never as ground truth. Do not use LiteLLM's zeros at all; there `0` means unset.\n- **Eight providers have no programmatic signal whatsoever** — NVIDIA, Cerebras, Google, DeepSeek, Groq, Mistral, Alibaba/DashScope, GitHub Copilot. Plus Nebius and Hyperbolic, which I could not verify and am declining to guess about.\n- **The strongest argument for your leave-empty rule is already in your own file:** b.ai advertises 42 models and serves 7; commandcode advertises 58 and serves 0; Venice serves a fully-priced catalogue and refuses every inference call. A models endpoint tells you what a provider *lists*, never what your key can *call*.\n\n**Files referenced:** `C:\\Users\\osami\\.llmkeys\\providers.json` (47 providers), `C:\\Users\\osami\\.llmkeys\\registry.json` (56 credentials; note it is UTF-8 **with BOM** — plain `json.load` fails, use `utf-8-sig`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3776,"cache_read_input_tokens":196530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3776,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CeeFBjseJwzjkfGh1Qccd","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"7a364620-0041-46d8-9bd7-0efb5912f449","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:51:28.997Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"7a364620-0041-46d8-9bd7-0efb5912f449","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"355cfc4f-9d72-4bb3-8805-f2dd57c05477","agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"The coordinator sent a message while you were working:\nScope refinement — new findings from a parallel agent, so you can avoid re-deriving them and focus where the real gap is.\n\nALREADY ESTABLISHED (treat as given, do not spend effort re-verifying):\n- models.dev (https://models.dev/api.json, MIT, 212 providers / 7,502 models, hourly bot sync, ETag support, npm mirror `@opencode-ai/models`) carries `cost{input,output,cache_read,cache_write,tiers}` for 7,066 models, plus `limit{context,output}`, `modalities`, `release_date`, `status: beta|deprecated`. It beats LiteLLM's model_prices json (131 providers / 3,518 models) for our case.\n- 594 models on models.dev have cost.input==0 && cost.output==0.\n- OpenRouter live: 421 models, 18 end in `:free` but 21 have zero price — so the `:free` suffix is already lossy against its own source of truth. Rule adopted: filter on price, never on id suffix.\n- \"Free\" is really THREE states, and conflating them misleads: (1) free pay-as-you-go but rate-limited, (2) zero-cost because a subscription/plan covers it (e.g. alibaba-token-plan 26/26, nvidia 99/103, zhipuai-coding-plan 9/10, gitlab 23/23), (3) genuinely paid.\n\nWHAT I NOW NEED FROM YOU — the gap models.dev does NOT close:\n\n1. Of our ~44 vault providers, roughly 23 are absent from the bundled catalogue and likely absent or thin on models.dev too. These are mostly small aggregators/routers: agentrouter, agnes, aionlabs, bai, bigmodel, bluesminds, commandcode, fanar, gmicloudai, gorouter, indeedwebid, llm7, nararouter, nousresearch, pollinations, routllm, seekai, tabiai, teamorouter, tokenharbor, tokenrouter, veniceai, xai. For AS MANY of these as you can verify from public docs: does their `/v1/models` response carry ANY price/free signal, or is the id-suffix convention the only thing available? Which of them use `:free` / `-free` / `/free`?\n\n2. For the \"subscription-covered\" category specifically: is there any programmatic way to distinguish state (2) from state (1)? Or must that be a curated per-provider annotation we maintain by hand?\n\n3. Rate-limit signals: which providers expose remaining quota / limits in response HEADERS (e.g. x-ratelimit-*)? A free-but-rate-limited model is materially different from a free unlimited one, and headers may be the only place that shows.\n\n4. Given all of the above, propose a concrete PRECEDENCE ORDER for deciding a model's free/paid label — e.g. explicit price data > provider-level curated annotation > id suffix > unknown — and say exactly when the answer must be left BLANK rather than guessed. The user's rule is explicit: if uncertain, leave empty, never say \"No\".\n\nKeep the per-provider capability table you were already building; this just re-points the effort at the uncovered providers rather than the well-documented majors.\n\nAddress this before completing your current task."},"isMeta":true,"uuid":"1e8b1773-3df0-40a9-9fd6-2e818b4f270c","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:51:30.234Z","origin":{"kind":"coordinator"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
