o-cost= 0 no-cost= 5\r\n\r\nmodels.dev ABSENT 16/23:\r\n   aionlabs, bai, bluesminds, commandcode, fanar, gorouter, indeedwebid, llm7, nararouter, nousresearch, pollinations, routllm, seekai, tabiai, teamorouter, tokenharbor","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f1a64606-4629-4731-b3e4-33322206beef","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"450ff9d4-cd49-4775-9c3a-2e0fdd1da85c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"bd9719e1-47b3-43ee-a40d-627915ec546e","agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CpZmMkiX92uhxYQLzrXCsB","type":"tool_result","content":"**Header names listed on the page (7 total):**\n\n| Header | Example value | Notes (per docs) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `retry-after` | 2 | \"In seconds\" |\n| `x-ratelimit-limit-requests` | 14400 | \"Always refers to Requests Per Day (RPD)\" |\n| `x-ratelimit-limit-tokens` | 18000 | \"Always refers to Tokens Per Minute (TPM)\" |\n| `x-ratelimit-remaining-requests` | 14370 | Requests Per Day |\n| `x-ratelimit-remaining-tokens` | 17997 | Tokens Per Minute |\n| `x-ratelimit-reset-requests` | 2m59.56s | Requests Per Day |\n| `x-ratelimit-reset-tokens` | 7.66s | Tokens Per Minute |\n\nThe docs note these values are \"illustrative.\"\n\n**When are they returned?**\n- `retry-after`: only on rate-limit rejections. The page states it \"is only set if you hit the rate limit and status code 429 is returned.\"\n- The other six: the docs say they are \"always included,\" which implies they accompany normal responses as well, not just 429s. Exceeding limits produces a `429 Too Many Requests`.\n\n**GET /v1/models?**\nNot addressed. The page only discusses \"HTTP response headers\" generically without scoping them to specific endpoints, so whether the models-listing endpoint carries them isn't determinable from this content.\n\n**Free tier differences / header visibility?**\nThe page shows separate tables for Free Plan and Developer Plan limits, so the underlying numeric limits do differ by plan — but the visible Free Plan table is the only one rendered here (e.g., `openai/gpt-oss-120b` at 30 RPM / 1K RPD / 8K TPM / 200K TPD). Nothing indicates the header *names* change by tier; only the values would reflect your org's actual limits.\n\n**Important caveats about coverage gaps:**\n- Only RPD and TPM are exposed via headers. Other tracked dimensions — TPD, ASH, ASD, ITPM, OTPM — have no corresponding headers documented, so daily-token and audio-second consumption can't be monitored this way.\n- Since limits apply \"at the organization level, not individual users,\" headers reflect org-wide consumption.\n- Cached tokens \"do not count towards your rate limits,\" so remaining-token figures should account for caching.\n- For ITPM/OTPM, the docs direct you to the limits page instead: hover over the TPM value for an \"X in / Y out\" breakdown; absence of a breakdown means a single combined TPM cap.\n\nFor exact current values, the docs repeatedly point to the limits page in account settings rather than treating the table as authoritative."}]},"uuid":"b20f4adb-3046-4da4-90e4-9c6baca98622","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:54:31.672Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":330591,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Header names listed on the page (7 total):**\n\n| Header | Example value | Notes (per docs) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `retry-after` | 2 | \"In seconds\" |\n| `x-ratelimit-limit-requests` | 14400 | \"Always refers to Requests Per Day (RPD)\" |\n| `x-ratelimit-limit-tokens` | 18000 | \"Always refers to Tokens Per Minute (TPM)\" |\n| `x-ratelimit-remaining-requests` | 14370 | Requests Per Day |\n| `x-ratelimit-remaining-tokens` | 17997 | Tokens Per Minute |\n| `x-ratelimit-reset-requests` | 2m59.56s | Requests Per Day |\n| `x-ratelimit-reset-tokens` | 7.66s | Tokens Per Minute |\n\nThe docs note these values are \"illustrative.\"\n\n**When are they returned?**\n- `retry-after`: only on rate-limit rejections. The page states it \"is only set if you hit the rate limit and status code 429 is returned.\"\n- The other six: the docs say they are \"always included,\" which implies they accompany normal responses as well, not just 429s. Exceeding limits produces a `429 Too Many Requests`.\n\n**GET /v1/models?**\nNot addressed. The page only discusses \"HTTP response headers\" generically without scoping them to specific endpoints, so whether the models-listing endpoint carries them isn't determinable from this content.\n\n**Free tier differences / header visibility?**\nThe page shows separate tables for Free Plan and Developer Plan limits, so the underlying numeric limits do differ by plan — but the visible Free Plan table is the only one rendered here (e.g., `openai/gpt-oss-120b` at 30 RPM / 1K RPD / 8K TPM / 200K TPD). Nothing indicates the header *names* change by tier; only the values would reflect your org's actual limits.\n\n**Important caveats about coverage gaps:**\n- Only RPD and TPM are exposed via headers. Other tracked dimensions — TPD, ASH, ASD, ITPM, OTPM — have no corresponding headers documented, so daily-token and audio-second consumption can't be monitored this way.\n- Since limits apply \"at the organization level, not individual users,\" headers reflect org-wide consumption.\n- Cached tokens \"do not count towards your rate limits,\" so remaining-token figures should account for caching.\n- For ITPM/OTPM, the docs direct you to the limits page instead: hover over the TPM value for an \"X in / Y out\" breakdown; absence of a breakdown means a single combined TPM cap.\n\nFor exact current values, the docs repeatedly point to the limits page in account settings rather than treating the table as authoritative.","durationMs":13201,"url":"https://console.groq.com/docs/rate-limits"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"450ff9d4-cd49-4775-9c3a-2e0fdd1da85c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
