{"parentUuid":"f9aa77ed-e4f8-492c-bd35-4850606510c6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","message":{"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeeFiomuYJLQ4mdg3FGSW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1679,"cache_read_input_tokens":229465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1679,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CeeFimVz8bK2TgxredMTg","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1699ad73-25e8-4d23-9a8e-11dcff6d1a6a","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:56:10.319Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
{"parentUuid":"1699ad73-25e8-4d23-9a8e-11dcff6d1a6a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a82676fb3de9cba9f","message":{"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeeFiomuYJLQ4mdg3FGSW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have what I need. Writing up.\n\n---\n\n# Free/Paid Determinability — Focused on the Uncovered Providers\n\n**Method:** unauthenticated `GET` probes only (no auth headers, no billed calls, no key values read). 19 small-provider `/v1/models` endpoints plus 10 `/api/pricing` endpoints probed live; docs used where endpoints returned 401/403. Everything below with a number attached is live-measured today, not recalled.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The 23 uncovered providers — what signal actually exists\n\n### 1a. Live probe results, `/v1/models`, unauthenticated\n\n| Provider | Status | Models | Price/free signal in response |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **nousresearch** | **200 public** | **378** | **Full OpenRouter-clone schema** + 2 extra fields (below) |\n| **routllm** | **200 public** | 12 | **`pricing{input,output,cache_read,cache_write}` USD/M + `tier_required`** |\n| **commandcode** | **200 public** | 62 | **None** — `id, object, created, owned_by, name, context_length` only |\n| agnes, bai, bigmodel, bluesminds, fanar, gmicloudai, indeedwebid, nararouter, seekai, teamorouter, tokenharbor, tokenrouter, xai | 401 | — | not probed further; docs give nothing per-model |\n| gorouter, tabiai | 403 (5.4 KB bot-challenge HTML) | — | WAF-blocked; your notes already warn a probe here is **not** cheap |\n| agentrouter | 401 (even with the WAF headers from your notes) | — | — |\n\n### 1b. The three that pay off\n\n**NousResearch — richest of the small providers, and it clones OpenRouter's schema exactly.**\n378 models with `id, canonical_slug, hugging_face_id, name, created, description, context_length, architecture, pricing, top_provider, supported_parameters, default_parameters, aliases, per_request_limits, supported_voices, knowledge_cutoff, expiration_date, links, reasoning, benchmarks, alias_target` — plus two fields OpenRouter does **not** have:\n\n- **`synthesizedFreeVariant: true`** on 5 models — an explicit boolean free flag.\n- **`pricing.original{prompt, completion, web_search, input_cache_read, input_cache_write}`** on **367/378** — the pre-discount upstream price. Nous is reselling below cost; `pricing.prompt` is what you pay, `pricing.original.prompt` is the list price.\n\nAgreement on Nous is perfect: 6 zero-priced, 6 `:free`-suffixed, **identical sets both directions**. The boolean covers only 5 of the 6 (`meituan/longcat-2.0:free` is zero-priced and suffixed but lacks the flag) — so **the flag is a subset of price, not a replacement for it.**\n\n**RoutLLM — carries both a price and a plan gate, which is the cleanest state-1/state-2 specimen I found.**\n\n```\ntier=1  anthropic/claude-fable-5     in=10    out=50\ntier=1  openai/gpt-5.6-luna          in=0.2   out=1.2\ntier=0  deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash   in=0.14  out=0.28\ntier=0  minimax/minimax-m2.7         in=0.3   out=1.2\n```\n\nEvery `tier_required: 0` model has a **non-zero** price. Your free-plan key can call them; the price is what a paid account is charged. Price alone says \"paid\" — correct for a cost column, wrong for \"can I use this at no charge\". Fields: `id, object, owned_by, display_name, context_window, max_output_tokens, tier_required, pricing{input,output,cache_read,cache_write}, capabilities{streaming,tools,vision,image_generation}`.\n\n**CommandCode — 62 models, publicly listable, and zero price information.** One `-free` id (`poolside/laguna-s-2.1-free`). The suffix is literally the only signal. And your own note records that all 62 return `400 insufficient credits` on a zero balance, so even the suffix is not an entitlement.\n\n### 1c. A second, better endpoint for the New-API-family gateways: **public `/api/pricing`**\n\nSeveral of these gateways run the open-source **New-API / One-API** codebase. That codebase exposes an **unauthenticated `/api/pricing`** route which `/v1/models` does not. Probed 10 bases; **3 returned 200 with no auth**:\n\n| Base | `/api/pricing` | Entries | Schema |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `https://api.tokenrouter.com` | **200, 62 KB** | 134 | New-API standard |\n| `https://agentrouter.org` | **200, 1.1 KB** | 5 | New-API standard |\n| `https://router.bynara.id` (nararouter) | **200, 27 KB** | 54 | custom, richer |\n| seekai 401 · tabitoken 403 · b.ai 403 · tokenharbor/teamorouter/ineed/aihubmix 404 | — | — | — |\n\n**New-API schema:** per entry `model_name, quota_type, model_ratio, completion_ratio, model_price, cache_ratio, create_cache_ratio, audio_ratio, enable_groups[], supported_endpoint_types[], vendor_id, tags, owner_by`; top level `group_ratio`, `usable_group`, `tiered_pricing`, `candidates_pricing`, `vendors`.\n\n**⚠️ The landmine you must not step on.** `model_price: 0` does **not** mean free. It is only used when `quota_type == 1` (per-call fixed pricing); for `quota_type == 0` billing runs off `model_ratio × group_ratio`. Measured:\n\n| | naive `model_price == 0` | correct test |\n|---|---|---|\n| tokenrouter | **123 of 134** | **3**: `z-ai/glm-5.3-free`, `nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni-30b-a3b-reasoning:free`, `stealth/ox-alpha` |\n| agentrouter | **5 of 5** (incl. `claude-opus-4-8` at `model_ratio: 4`) | **0** |\n\nThe correct predicate is:\n```\n(quota_type == 0 && model_ratio == 0) || (quota_type == 1 && model_price == 0)\n```\nA naive parser would label **every Claude Opus model on agentrouter as free.**\n\nNote `stealth/ox-alpha` — genuinely free, **no suffix**. Another recall failure for the id convention.\n\n**Nara Router publishes a custom schema that directly encodes the subscription-covered state** — the single most useful find for your question 2:\n\n`alias, display_name, input_credit_per_1k, output_credit_per_1k, cache_read_credit_per_1k, supports_streaming, supports_vision, supports_image_generation, supports_video_generation, reasoning, max_context_tokens, payg_enabled, ` **`free_for_paid`** `, ` **`free_min_balance`** `, quota_weight, quota_weight_input, quota_weight_cache, official_in_usd_m, official_out_usd_m`; top level `usd_to_idr: 17765`.\n\n```\nfree_for_paid=True (6 models) — every one has a NON-ZERO credit price:\n  deepseek-v4-flash-free   in=0.157  out=0.315   free_min_balance=10000\n  glm-5.3-flash-free       in=0.266  out=0.887   free_min_balance=10000\n  glm-5.3-free             in=7.435  out=23.366  free_min_balance=15000\n  glm-5.2-promo            in=5.125  out=16.106  free_min_balance=30000\n  mimo-v2.5-free           in=0.150  out=1.501   free_min_balance=10000\n  qwen3.8-flash-free       in=0.799  out=2.502   free_min_balance=5000\n```\n\nFree **conditional on holding a minimum balance**. The `-free` suffix is present; the price says paid; the truth is neither. This is exactly the case your rule exists for.\n\nAnd the 5 genuinely zero-credit Nara models are all **image/video**: `agnes-image-2.0-flash`, `agnes-image-2.1-flash`, `agnes-video-v2.0`, `grok-imagine`, `nano-banana-pro`. **Zero *token* price on a non-text-output model means \"billed per image/second in a different unit\", not free.** That generalizes — apply it as a guard everywhere.\n\n### 1d. Suffix convention across the 23\n\n| Convention | Providers (evidence) |\n|---|---|\n| `:free` | nousresearch (6, live-verified, perfect price agreement), tokenharbor, tokenrouter (mixed with `-free`) |\n| `-free` | tokenrouter, nararouter, teamorouter, commandcode (1), bai, seekai |\n| `/free` | gorouter — n/a; none of the 23 use `/free` (that's orcarouter/kilo, outside this set) |\n| `-promo` | nararouter — same semantics as its `-free`, i.e. **state 2** |\n| **No suffix, genuinely free** | tokenrouter `stealth/ox-alpha`; gmicloudai (uses `is_free` flag); agnes (platform-wide free, per your notes) |\n| **Suffix, NOT free** | **nararouter — all 6, priced + balance-gated**; pollinations community re-exports (`AkshayCoder48/meituan-longcat-2.0-free` has non-zero pollen price; several `:free` ids carry **no price fields at all**) |\n| **Provider uses \"free\" for the ACCOUNT PLAN, not models** | routllm (`tier_required`), llm7 (`tier` ∈ {pro, turbo} — **no `free` value exists** in 44 models) |\n\n### 1e. models.dev coverage of these 23 — **7 of 23**\n\n| Covered | models.dev id | models | zero-cost |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| agentrouter | `agentrouter` | 3 | 0 (all 3 have **no** `cost` field) |\n| agnes | `agnes` | 3 | 2 (`agnes-2.0-flash`, `agnes-2.5-flash`) |\n| bigmodel | `zhipuai` | 15 | 2 (`glm-4.7-flash`, `glm-4.5-flash`) |\n| gmicloudai | `gmicloud` | 15 | 0 — **contradicts** the provider's own `is_free` flag, which your notes record as true for MiniMax-M3 / M2.7 |\n| tokenrouter | `tokenrouter` | 1 | 1 (`z-ai/glm-5.3-free`) — matches my live `/api/pricing`, but only **1 of 134** models indexed |\n| veniceai | `venice` | 101 | 0 |\n| xai | `xai` | 12 | 0 (5 have no `cost`) |\n\n**Absent from models.dev (16 of 23):** aionlabs, bai, bluesminds, commandcode, fanar, gorouter, indeedwebid, llm7, nararouter, nousresearch, pollinations, routllm, seekai, tabiai, teamorouter, tokenharbor.\n\nTwo calibration warnings: models.dev's **tokenrouter coverage is 1/134** — presence in the catalogue does not mean useful coverage; and its **gmicloud entry disagrees with gmicloud's own `is_free` flag**. First-party beats models.dev whenever both exist.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Distinguishing state (2) \"subscription-covered\" from state (1) \"free PAYG\"\n\n**Programmatically, for a handful of providers — yes. Generally — no. It must be a curated per-provider annotation.**\n\nProviders that expose a machine-readable state-2 discriminator (all live-verified):\n\n| Provider | Field | Semantics |\n|---|---|---|\n| **nararouter** | `free_for_paid` (bool) + `free_min_balance` (int) | free iff balance ≥ threshold; price stays non-zero |\n| **routllm** | `tier_required` (0/1) | 0 = included in the free account plan, priced anyway |\n| **New-API family** (tokenrouter, agentrouter, …) | `enable_groups[]` + top-level `group_ratio` | your key's group determines the multiplier; `group_ratio` can be 0 |\n| **OpenRouter** | `GET /api/v1/key` → `is_free_tier` | account-level only, not per model; requires auth |\n| **huggingface** | `providers[].is_free` | true state-1 flag, but currently 0/314 true |\n| **nousresearch** | `synthesizedFreeVariant` | marks a free variant *derived* from a paid model |\n\nEverywhere else there is nothing. The structural reason: state 2 is a property of **(model × your account's plan/balance/group)**, and a models endpoint is keyed on model alone. Cloudflare is the clean illustration — 10,000 Neurons/day free on both Workers Free and Paid, yet `@cf/moonshotai/kimi-k2.6`, `@cf/zai-org/glm-5.2` and `@cf/deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-pro-0813` require paid billing regardless, and that carve-out exists **only in an HTML doc table**.\n\n**Recommendation:** carry state as a small enum on the *model* row, not a boolean — and let a hand-maintained provider-level annotation supply it when the API cannot:\n\n```\nfree_state ∈ { zero_price, plan_covered, quota_covered, paid, unknown }\nfree_state_source ∈ { api_price, api_flag, api_plan_field, curated, absent }\nfree_state_verified_at : timestamp\n```\n\nThe curated annotation is unavoidable for at least: cloudflare, ollama-cloud, google, groq, nvidia, cerebras, opencode (time-limited promo), agnes (\"currently free\"), aihubmix, huggingface (monthly credit allowance). Give every curated entry an expiry — opencode's promo list and agnes's free-platform status are both dated 2026-08 in your notes and neither has a machine-readable end date anywhere.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Rate-limit headers\n\n**Measured, and the answer is unambiguous: no `/v1/models` endpoint returns rate-limit headers.**\n\nI captured full response headers on all 19 small-provider probes and re-probed 12 majors (openrouter, huggingface, novita, pollinations, venice, chutes, llm7, groq, together, mistral, xai, cerebras) with `-D -`, grepping for `ratelimit|rate-limit|retry-after|x-credit`. **Zero matches, on 200s and on 401s alike.**\n\nRate-limit headers live on **inference** endpoints only:\n\n| Provider | Headers | When |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Groq** | `x-ratelimit-limit-requests` (RPD), `x-ratelimit-limit-tokens` (TPM), `x-ratelimit-remaining-requests`, `x-ratelimit-remaining-tokens`, `x-ratelimit-reset-requests`, `x-ratelimit-reset-tokens` — docs say \"always included\"; `retry-after` on 429 only | chat/completions |\n| **OpenRouter** | `X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, `X-RateLimit-Reset`, `Retry-After` — **429 responses only**; successful responses carry none | chat/completions |\n| OpenAI / Anthropic / Mistral / Cerebras | `x-ratelimit-*` families (documented, not probed) | chat/completions |\n\n**Consequence for your design:** headers are useless as a catalogue-build signal, because reading them requires the billed call you are trying to avoid. Groq's headers are the *only* place its free-tier state is visible, and they cost a call to see — which is precisely why Groq must be blank.\n\nTwo non-header quota signals that *are* free to read:\n- **Pollinations** — `per_user_rpm` on 210/362 models, in the models response itself.\n- **OpenRouter** — `GET /api/v1/key` (`limit_remaining`, `usage_daily`, `is_free_tier`) — auth required but not billed.\n\nIf you want rate-limit tiering in the catalogue, model it as a **separate, optional, hand-curated column** (`rate_limit_note`), never as a derived field.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Proposed precedence order\n\nEvaluate top-down; **first rule that fires wins**; if none fires, the field is **BLANK**.\n\n```\nP0  GUARDS — force BLANK regardless of anything below\n    G1  output_modalities contains image/audio/video AND the zero price is a *token* price\n        → billed in a different unit. (nararouter: agnes-image-*, grok-imagine, nano-banana-pro)\n    G2  New-API source AND quota_type == 0 AND only model_price == 0 was checked\n        → invalid test; 123/134 tokenrouter, 5/5 agentrouter false-positive.\n    G3  Model id matches a known internal/staging pattern (ai_infer_test_*, dev/*, gt-4p, bunny)\n        or carries a non-available status (novita status==4, fireworks state!=READY).\n    G4  Provider is on the \"catalogue lies\" list (b.ai, commandcode, veniceai, indeedwebid,\n        tabiai, gorouter) → catalogue listing is not an entitlement; blank unless a dated\n        live probe exists.\n\nP1  FIRST-PARTY EXPLICIT ZERO PRICE  → free = true\n    Both input and output token prices present AND both == 0.\n    Sources: openrouter pricing.prompt/completion · nousresearch (same) · novita\n    input_token_price_per_m/output_token_price_per_m · venice model_spec.pricing.*.usd ·\n    chutes pricing.prompt/completion · together pricing.input/output · sambanova ·\n    aionlabs · llm7 pricing.input/output · routllm pricing.input/output ·\n    New-API (quota_type==0 && model_ratio==0) || (quota_type==1 && model_price==0)\n\nP2  FIRST-PARTY EXPLICIT BOOLEAN FLAG  → free = true\n    gmicloudai is_free · huggingface providers[].is_free · nousresearch synthesizedFreeVariant\n    Rank below P1 because on Nous the flag covers 5 of 6 zero-priced models — it under-reports.\n\nP3  FIRST-PARTY PLAN/BALANCE FIELD  → free_state = plan_covered, free = BLANK\n    nararouter free_for_paid + free_min_balance · routllm tier_required==0 ·\n    New-API enable_groups + group_ratio==0\n    These are NOT \"free\" in a price column. Record the state; leave the boolean empty.\n\nP4  CURATED PROVIDER ANNOTATION with a live-probe date  → free = true, confidence=medium\n    Requires: named model ids, a verified_at timestamp, and an expiry.\n    (opencode's 7 promo models; agnes platform-free; gmicloud's probed pair.)\n    Expired annotation → demote to BLANK, never to false.\n\nP5  THIRD-PARTY CATALOGUE (models.dev)  → free = true, confidence=low, needs confirmation\n    Only when cost{input,output} are BOTH present AND both == 0.\n    Never when the cost field is absent (ollama 22/22, agentrouter 3/3).\n    Never for nvidia (99/103 zeros encode a credits grant, not a token price).\n    Never import LiteLLM zeros at all — there 0 means \"unset\" (130 entries, mostly rerank/LoRA).\n    Provider-level disagreement with a first-party flag → first-party wins (gmicloud).\n\nP6  ID SUFFIX (:free / -free / /free) ALONE  → free = BLANK, flag for review\n    Measured precision by provider: openrouter 18/18, nousresearch 6/6, tokenrouter 2/2 —\n    but nararouter 0/6 and pollinations 0/13. The convention is only trustworthy where a\n    price feed has already confirmed it, at which point P1 already answered.\n    Never promote a suffix to `true` on a provider with no price feed.\n\nP7  NOTHING FIRED  → BLANK\n```\n\n### When the answer must be BLANK — explicit list\n\n**Never write `No`/`false` for any of these. Leave the cell empty.**\n\n1. **No price field exists anywhere in the response.** NVIDIA NIM (82 models, 4 fields), Cerebras, Groq, DeepSeek, Google Gemini, Mistral, Alibaba/DashScope, **commandcode** (62 models, no price), GitHub Copilot (no endpoint at all).\n2. **Endpoint unreachable / schema unverified.** Nebius, Hyperbolic — I could not confirm either and am not guessing. gorouter, tabiai — WAF-blocked, and your notes warn a probe there bills real Opus usage.\n3. **Price present but partial.** HuggingFace's 106/314 provider rows with no `pricing` dict — `is_free: false` there is asserted without a price behind it.\n4. **Non-USD unit with no conversion.** Pollinations (pollen), Cloudflare (Neurons), nararouter credits (`usd_to_idr` is a display rate, not a token price), Chutes TAO.\n5. **Zero token price on a non-text-output model.** Guard G1.\n6. **Plan- or balance-gated.** Guard P3 — record `plan_covered`, leave the boolean empty.\n7. **Catalogue known not to reflect entitlement.** Guard G4.\n8. **Suffix is the only evidence.** P6.\n9. **Curated annotation past its expiry.**\n\n### Where `false` IS safe\n\nOnly when a first-party price feed returned **both** token prices and at least one is non-zero, for a text-output model, from a provider not on the G4 list. That covers openrouter, nousresearch, novita (status 1), venice, chutes, together, sambanova, aionlabs, llm7, routllm, and correctly-parsed New-API gateways — and nowhere else.\n\n---\n\n## Revised per-provider capability table (the 23, plus corrections)\n\nReliability: **A** = first-party per-model price · **B** = first-party boolean flag · **P** = first-party plan/balance field · **C** = suffix only · **✗** = no signal\n\n| Provider | Best endpoint | Signal | Rel. | Populate `free`? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **nousresearch** | `/v1/models` (public) | `pricing.prompt/completion` + `synthesizedFreeVariant` + `pricing.original` | **A+B** | **Yes** — 6 free, price and suffix agree perfectly |\n| **routllm** | `/v1/models` (public) | `pricing{in,out,cache}` + `tier_required` | **A+P** | Price → all paid. Set `plan_covered` for the 5 `tier_required:0` |\n| **tokenrouter** | **`/api/pricing`** (public) | `quota_type`+`model_ratio` | **A** | **Yes** — 3 free (incl. unsuffixed `stealth/ox-alpha`) |\n| **agentrouter** | **`/api/pricing`** (public) | same | **A** | **Yes** → 0 free. `model_price:0` is a trap here |\n| **nararouter** | **`/api/pricing`** (public) | credits + `free_for_paid` + `free_min_balance` | **A+P** | **Blank** for boolean; set `plan_covered` on the 6 |\n| **commandcode** | `/v1/models` (public) | none | **✗** | **Blank** (+ G4: nothing callable at $0) |\n| gmicloudai | `/v1/models` (auth) | `is_free` per model | **B** | Yes (your probe: MiniMax-M3, M2.7) — overrides models.dev |\n| veniceai | `/api/v1/models` (public) | `model_spec.pricing.*.usd` | **A** | Yes → none free (+ G4: $0 balance blocks inference) |\n| llm7 | `/v1/models` (public) | `pricing.input/output`, `tier`∈{pro,turbo} | **A** | Yes → all paid; no `free` tier value exists |\n| aionlabs | `/v1/models` (public, key = `models`) | `pricing` + `expires_at` + `replacement_model_id` | **A** | Yes → none free |\n| pollinations | `/v1/models` (public) | pollen only; suffixed ids priced or unpriced | **✗** | **Blank** |\n| bigmodel | 401 | models.dev: 2 zero-cost | **P5** | Low confidence; confirm before use |\n| agnes | 401 | models.dev 2 zero-cost + \"currently free\" note | **P4/P5** | Yes with expiry |\n| xai | 401 | models.dev 12/0 zero | **P5** | Blank or `false` only via P5 |\n| bai | 401 | — (+ G4: 7 of 42 callable) | **✗** | **Blank** |\n| seekai | 401 (`/api/pricing` 401 too) | New-API, no public feed | **✗** | **Blank** |\n| tabiai, gorouter | 403 WAF | — | **✗** | **Blank — do not probe** |\n| teamorouter, tokenharbor, indeedwebid, bluesminds, fanar | 401, no public pricing feed | suffix only (first three) | **C/✗** | **Blank** |\n\n**Correction to my earlier report:** I previously classed routllm as \"tier gate, not price\". It carries **both** — full USD/M pricing *and* `tier_required`. And I had not found the New-API `/api/pricing` route, which converts tokenrouter, agentrouter and nararouter from \"suffix only\" to \"first-party price data\".\n\n---\n\n## Three things worth acting on\n\n1. **Add `/api/pricing` to the fetch plan for every New-API-family gateway** — it is unauthenticated, and it is the only price source for gateways whose `/v1/models` is auth-walled. Probe it for seekai, tabitoken, b.ai, tokenharbor, teamorouter, ineed, aihubmix on a schedule; they may open up.\n2. **Encode the New-API predicate correctly or you will mislabel Claude Opus as free.** `model_price == 0` alone gives a 100% false-positive rate on agentrouter and 92% on tokenrouter.\n3. **`free_state` must be an enum, not a boolean.** Nara Router publishes six models that are simultaneously suffixed `-free`, non-zero-priced, and genuinely free above a balance threshold. No boolean can represent that honestly — and a boolean forced to `false` there would be exactly the wrong answer your rule is designed to prevent."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1679,"cache_read_input_tokens":229465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1679,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CeeFimVz8bK2TgxredMTg","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"926149bf-a4f5-436f-bf2a-8f5370964997","timestamp":"2026-09-02T07:58:02.781Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\osami\\.uw\\keysync","sessionId":"76ac34d9-c9e8-43f4-8cfa-18bf9783c39c","version":"2.1.257","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"curious-crafting-coral"}
